(2264,	20,	'block_1_h2',	'Using Briz'),
(2265,	20,	'_block_1_h2',	'field_5caf3b5bbbe42'),
(2266,	20,	'block_1_questions_0_question',	'How can I find e-scooters?'),
(2267,	20,	'_block_1_questions_0_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2268,	20,	'block_1_questions_0_answer',	'Launch the app and check for available e-scooters on the map. Once you select a vehicle\r\nthe map will give you directions to its location. Alternatively, you can just pick any vehicle\r\nyou see on the street and scan its QR code to unlock it.'),
(2269,	20,	'_block_1_questions_0_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2270,	20,	'block_1_questions_1_question',	'Unlocking'),
(2271,	20,	'_block_1_questions_1_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2272,	20,	'block_1_questions_1_answer',	'Once you find an e-scooter on the map you can unlock it by either <b>scanning the QR\r\ncode</b> or typing in the plate number. Tapping the flashlight icon will turn on the flashlight if\r\nthe QR code scanner is having trouble reading the code in low light.'),
(2273,	20,	'_block_1_questions_1_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2274,	20,	'block_1_questions_2_question',	'Adjusting and Starting'),
(2275,	20,	'_block_1_questions_2_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2276,	20,	'block_1_questions_2_answer',	'First, kick off and build up some speed. When you’re moving under your own power you\r\ncan accelerate by depressing the throttle near your right thumb. Get comfortable at low\r\nspeeds first and squeeze the brake to slow down when necessary.'),
(2277,	20,	'_block_1_questions_2_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2278,	20,	'block_1_questions_3_question',	'Ride'),
(2279,	20,	'_block_1_questions_3_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2280,	20,	'block_1_questions_3_answer',	'Keep both feet on the E-Scooter while riding. Ride in bike lanes where available,\r\ndo not ride on sidewalks. You can push the brake button with your left thumb to\r\nslow down if needed.'),
(2281,	20,	'_block_1_questions_3_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2282,	20,	'block_1_questions_4_question',	'Parking'),
(2283,	20,	'_block_1_questions_4_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2284,	20,	'block_1_questions_4_answer',	'To keep yourself and others safe, please ensure that you park in designated areas. Scooter\r\nparking areas are available in some cities; otherwise, please check the in-app map for\r\nplaces to park. This makes it easier for other riders to find the scooter later. Be considerate\r\nof others and don’t park too far away from accessible pedestrian walkways. Additionally,\r\nbe careful not to park in no-parking zones, including wheelchair ramps, blocking streets or\r\nsidewalks, hospital entrances, fire stations, gated communities, and locations with no phone\r\nservice, among others.'),
(2285,	20,	'_block_1_questions_4_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2286,	20,	'block_1_questions_5_question',	'Unlocking More Than One Vehicle'),
(2287,	20,	'_block_1_questions_5_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2288,	20,	'block_1_questions_5_answer',	'Only one vehicle per account can be unlocked at a time, and the rider whose account is\r\nused to unlock the vehicle must be the only person who rides it. Any damage caused by\r\nthird-party riders will be attributed to the account-holder.'),
(2289,	20,	'_block_1_questions_5_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2290,	20,	'block_1_questions_6_question',	'Pausing your Ride'),
(2291,	20,	'_block_1_questions_6_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2292,	20,	'block_1_questions_6_answer',	'You can temporarily stop your ride, keeping your vehicle reserved until you want to\r\nresume your trip. <b>The per-minute charge will continue to accumulate while the e-\r\nscooter is paused.</b><br>\r\nTapping “<b>End Ride</b>” will stop the per-minute charges, and will make the vehicle available\r\nto other users. If you do not end the ride, the charges will continue, so make sure you end it\r\nonce you are done!'),
(2293,	20,	'_block_1_questions_6_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2294,	20,	'block_1_questions_7_question',	'Stop for more than 10 minutes'),
(2295,	20,	'_block_1_questions_7_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2296,	20,	'block_1_questions_7_answer',	'During your ride, if the E-Scooter is not moving for more than 10 minutes, the\r\nmotor will turn off automatically. Please click the “Continue to Ride” button in the\r\napp to unlock and continue your rides.'),
(2297,	20,	'_block_1_questions_7_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2298,	20,	'block_1_questions_8_question',	'End Ride'),
(2299,	20,	'_block_1_questions_8_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2300,	20,	'block_1_questions_8_answer',	'End your ride by clicking “Lock” in the app. Confirm that you have parked within the\r\noperating area. If you do not park within the operating area, you will be fined.<br>\r\nTapping “<b>End Ride</b>” will stop the per-minute charges, and will make the vehicle available\r\nto other users. If you do not end the ride, the charges will continue, so make sure you end it\r\nonce you are done!'),
(2301,	20,	'_block_1_questions_8_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2302,	20,	'block_1_questions_9_question',	'Operating area'),
(2303,	20,	'_block_1_questions_9_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2304,	20,	'block_1_questions_9_answer',	'Please check the map to see the operating area in your city.\r\n\r\nYou can start and end your ride wherever you want within the operating area in the\r\nsame region displayed without any surcharges. During your ride, you can leave the\r\noperating area. Just make sure you finish your ride in the operating area.\r\nPlease make sure you park your E-Scooter properly. If you park your E-Scooter\r\noutside the operating area, retrieval service charges may incur for you.'),
(2305,	20,	'_block_1_questions_9_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2306,	20,	'block_1_questions_10_question',	'Operating\r\nhours'),
(2307,	20,	'_block_1_questions_10_question',	'field_5caf3b3ebbe40'),
(2308,	20,	'block_1_questions_10_answer',	'BRiZ scooters will be available every day from 4 a.m. until 9 p.m. Because scooters need to be recharged on a nightly basis and ours are designed to not have swappable batteries, our operations team and chargers team will be responsible for removing dead-battery scooters from the streets and redeploying them the following morning.'),
(2309,	20,	'_block_1_questions_10_answer',	'field_5caf3b46bbe41'),
(2310,	20,	'block_1_questions',	'12'),
(2311,	20,	'_block_1_questions',	'field_5caf3b2cbbe3f'),
