(181,	1,	'2019-05-14 16:27:59',	'2019-05-14 13:27:59',	'<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why now? </span>\n\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">World cities become more urban and streets more crowded.\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">People spend an insane amount of time in traffic.\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Businesses lose enormous amount of money annually.\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Traffic jams affect air quality.\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO2 emissions have increased on an annual basis.\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Carbon dioxide contributes to climate change.\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The need for mobility innovations is in demand. </span>\n\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why BRiZ? </span>\n\n&nbsp;\n\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">BRiZ is a micro-mobility share company.</span>\n\n&nbsp;\n\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our core is green. </span>\n\n&nbsp;\n\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We deliver mobility to everyone around the world while minimizing the impact on the environment. </span>\n\n&nbsp;\n\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We offer the most flexible, cheap and fun urban transport dedicated to reducing traffic congestions and CO2 emissions.</span>\n\n&nbsp;\n\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We are reinventing shared mobility using blockchain and smart contracts.</span>\n\n&nbsp;\n\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We strive to transform both our cities and our world into better, safer and healthier places. </span>',	'Our Mission',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'16-autosave-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 16:27:59',	'2019-05-14 13:27:59',	'',	16,	'https://briz.app/16-autosave-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(182,	1,	'2019-05-14 16:28:43',	'2019-05-14 13:28:43',	'<h2><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why now? </span></h2>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">World cities become more urban and streets more crowded.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">People spend an insane amount of time in traffic.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Businesses lose enormous amount of money annually.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Traffic jams affect air quality.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CO2 emissions have increased on an annual basis.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Carbon dioxide contributes to climate change.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The need for mobility innovations is in demand. </span>\r\n<h2><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why BRiZ? </span></h2>\r\n<h3><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">BRiZ is a micro-mobility share company.</span></h3>\r\n<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Our core is green.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We deliver mobility to everyone around the world while minimizing the impact on the environment.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We offer the most flexible, cheap and fun urban transport dedicated to reducing traffic congestions and CO2 emissions.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We are reinventing shared mobility using blockchain and smart contracts.\r\n</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">We strive to transform both our cities and our world into better, safer and healthier places. </span>',	'Our Mission',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'16-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 16:28:43',	'2019-05-14 13:28:43',	'',	16,	'https://briz.app/16-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(183,	1,	'2019-05-21 00:49:36',	'2019-05-20 21:49:36',	'<h3><strong>Company Address</strong></h3>\nBRIZ MOBILITY LIMITED\nClifton House\nFitzwilliam Street\nLower, Dublin\nD02 XT91, Ireland\n\n<strong>Contact</strong>\n<div class=\"page\" title=\"Page 3\">\n<div class=\"section\">\n<div class=\"layoutArea\">\n<div class=\"column\">\n\n24/7 BRiZ Customer Service and Support\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\nE-Mail: <a href=\"mailto:hello@briz.app\">hello@briz.app</a>\nPhone: +41800322013\nHelp Desk: https://www.briz.app/contact',	'Legal Notice',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'160-autosave-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-21 00:49:36',	'2019-05-20 21:49:36',	'',	160,	'https://briz.app/160-autosave-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(184,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:02:43',	'2019-05-14 14:02:43',	'<h2><strong>Company Address</strong></h2>\r\nBRIZ MOBILITY LIMITED\r\nClifton House\r\nFitzwilliam Street\r\nLower, Dublin\r\nD02 XT91, Ireland\r\n\r\n<strong>Contact</strong>\r\nE-Mail: <a href=\"mailto:hello@briz.app\">hello@briz.app</a>\r\n<strong>For customer support inquiries:</strong> <a href=\"https://www.briz.app/contact\">https://www.briz.app/contact</a>\r\n<strong>For press inquiries:</strong> <a href=\"mailto:press@briz.app\">press@briz.app</a>',	'Legal notice',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'160-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:02:43',	'2019-05-14 14:02:43',	'',	160,	'https://briz.app/160-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(185,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:38:01',	'2019-05-14 14:38:01',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\n\n<strong>Content\n</strong>\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\n\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\n\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\n\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\n\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\n\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\n\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\n\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\n\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\n\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\n\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\n\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\n\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\n\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\n\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\n\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\n\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\n\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\n\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\n\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\n\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\n\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\n\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\n\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\n\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\n\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\n\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\n\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\n\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\n\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\n\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\n\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\n\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\n\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\n\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\n\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\n\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\n\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\n\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\n\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\n\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\n\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\n\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\n\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\n\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\n\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\n\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\n\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\n\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\n\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\nrental date.\n\n<strong>4.6 Prohibited Use</strong>\n\nThe vehicles must not be used:\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\nj) For any commercial purposes;\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\n\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\n\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\n\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\n\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\n\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet connection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the contact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ Rental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\n\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ with information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\n\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific conditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other road or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at trees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property of third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire department service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access paths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian crossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle covers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered item is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the areas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and, in general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are driving the Vehicle.\n\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related holding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are also not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the affected area.\n\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you for any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if the Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will continue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions, but no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The corresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are not responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the damage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\n\n<strong>6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing</strong>\n\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App. In addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins. BRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in accordance with section 10 of these ToS.\n\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to the current Price List (hyperlink).\n\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as indicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\n\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract. Payments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract month or contract year.\n\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you may charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as your preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit card (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses the _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information see section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you will be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to confirm.\n\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account, the Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other payments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion provide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately by BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your Credit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a balance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and insofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the amounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the (remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\n\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ App or any other third party.\n\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event of termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a designated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any remaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor may these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\n\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by law (e.g. value added tax).\n\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the applicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove that no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\n\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet your payment obligations.\n\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such recoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\n\n<strong>7. Term and Termination</strong>\n\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\n\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle Rental or a Subscription.\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App notification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a termination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees within 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you communicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to section 17 of these ToS.\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in accordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\n\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right The extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1 and 7.2 of these ToS\n\n<strong>8. Liability and Limitation of Liability</strong>\n\n<strong>8.1 Your Liability</strong>\n\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to theft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of slight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric Scooter.\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of these ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the Price List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment has occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ reserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and agents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses arising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS, (ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to Other Drivers.\n\n<strong>8.2 BRIZ’s Liability</strong>\n\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties (“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal Obligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the contractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper performance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and trust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not result in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of the typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages resulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious agents.\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is excluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3. BRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of force majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the customer immediately if necessary.\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions, this shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents of BRIZ.\n\n<strong>9. Privacy Notice</strong>\n\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules and to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\n\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit card, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered in England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license Nr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose payment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter will be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit card transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here: <a href=\"https://payally.eu/privacy-policy\">https://payally.eu/privacy-policy</a>. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\n\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your personal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\n\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your personal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\n\n<strong>10. Changes to these ToS and Prices</strong>\n\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in accordance with the following terms.\n\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without giving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at least three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions that (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will remain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\n\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month. All notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned consequences in the change notification.\n\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned consequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a change in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with effect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do not object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will particularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If mandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above deadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the current contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force. However, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual Subscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three days.\n\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or notification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\n\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also applies to this text form requirement.\n\n<strong>11. Content of Third Parties</strong>\n\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or sponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third party services.\n\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the BRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\n\n<strong>12. Applicable Law</strong>\n\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the laws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\n\n<strong>13. Transfer</strong>\n\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third party at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time before such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\n\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to third parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\n\n<strong>14. No Waiver</strong>\n\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these ToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these ToS.\n\n<strong>15. Validity</strong>\n\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared invalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or Price List (hyperlink).\n\n<strong>16. Remark of Dispute</strong>\n\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a Federal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution Platform <a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage\">https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage</a> on alternative dispute resolution.\n\n<strong>17. Customer Service</strong>\n\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through the BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-mail (hello@briz.app).\n\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-autosave-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:38:01',	'2019-05-14 14:38:01',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-autosave-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(186,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:09:49',	'2019-05-14 14:09:49',	'Terms of Service\r\nLast updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility\r\nLimited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”,\r\n“our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland\r\n(“you”, “your”).\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental\r\nContract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a\r\nSubscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these\r\nToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as\r\namended from time to time.\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of\r\nthese ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers\r\nwho wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country\r\nis the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\nBRIZ App means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android\r\nand iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\nBRIZ Website means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\nBRIZ Rental Contract means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each\r\nSingle Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\nForce Majeure Event means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the\r\ncontrol of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods,\r\nearthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other\r\nelements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection,\r\nriots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-\r\nouts, and civil unrest.\r\nSingle Vehicle Rental means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the\r\nconfirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS.\r\nOther Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your\r\nauthorization.\r\n\r\nOperating Area means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally\r\nbe rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nRental Time means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in\r\naccordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental\r\nContract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\nServices means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles\r\ntogether with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in\r\nyour country of residence.\r\nSubscription means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a\r\ncertain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or\r\nannual pass subscription).\r\nToS means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each\r\nBRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nVehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n2. Contractual Object\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time\r\nto time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles\r\nmade available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may\r\nbe, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List\r\n(hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your\r\nlocation will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are\r\nand remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The\r\ncountries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n3. BRIZ App and Website; Account\r\nYou can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online\r\napplication stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n3.1 Registration\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When\r\nregistering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also\r\nregister via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years\r\nof age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account,\r\nthrough which you can rent vehicles.\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to\r\nkeep it up to date.\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in\r\nparticular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may\r\nonly be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use\r\nthe BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access\r\ndata. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using\r\nyour account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable\r\nfor any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use\r\nwas caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access\r\ndata by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided\r\nat the end of these ToS.\r\n3.2 Network Access and Device\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use\r\nthe Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your\r\nInternet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are\r\nresponsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile\r\nnetworks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the\r\ncontrol of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on\r\nall devices.\r\n3.3 Notifications\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text\r\nmessages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation.\r\nAdvertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n4. Single Vehicle Rental\r\n4.1 Rental Period\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle\r\nthrough the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental\r\nthe electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of\r\nthese ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time\r\nthe vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the\r\nextent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you\r\nrent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are\r\nresponsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are\r\nliable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as\r\nyour own responsibility.\r\n4.2 Availability; Maintenance\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ\r\nstrives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be\r\nadequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ\r\nguarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n4.3 Terms of Use\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree\r\nthat:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is\r\nlegally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes,\r\nand laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case\r\nmay be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists,\r\npedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are\r\nnot relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the\r\nrisk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any\r\nresulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation\r\nduring the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other\r\nreasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using\r\nthe Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of\r\nBRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a\r\nvehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject\r\nto additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the\r\nlocal police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving\r\nnot only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or\r\n\r\nstolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ\r\narising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n4.5 Checking the Vehicle\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front\r\nand rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these\r\nToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical\r\ndefect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness.\r\nBRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect\r\nthat may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to\r\nsection 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from\r\ndamage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of\r\nage, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental\r\ncondition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the\r\nability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol,\r\ndrugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate\r\nthe Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that\r\nmay distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or\r\nthunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s\r\nroadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are\r\nusing the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-\r\nroad trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a\r\nVehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be\r\nfreely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric\r\nScooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within\r\nthe boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the\r\nBRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List\r\n(hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you\r\ncan view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the\r\nBRIZ app.\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:09:49',	'2019-05-14 14:09:49',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(187,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:10:33',	'2019-05-14 14:10:33',	'Terms of Service\r\nLast updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\nBRIZ App means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android\r\nand iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\nBRIZ Website means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\nBRIZ Rental Contract means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each\r\nSingle Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\nForce Majeure Event means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the\r\ncontrol of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods,\r\nearthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other\r\nelements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection,\r\nriots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-\r\nouts, and civil unrest.\r\nSingle Vehicle Rental means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the\r\nconfirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS.\r\nOther Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your\r\nauthorization.\r\n\r\nOperating Area means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally\r\nbe rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nRental Time means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in\r\naccordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental\r\nContract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\nServices means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles\r\ntogether with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in\r\nyour country of residence.\r\nSubscription means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a\r\ncertain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or\r\nannual pass subscription).\r\nToS means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each\r\nBRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nVehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n2. Contractual Object\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time\r\nto time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles\r\nmade available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may\r\nbe, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List\r\n(hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your\r\nlocation will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are\r\nand remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The\r\ncountries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n3. BRIZ App and Website; Account\r\nYou can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online\r\napplication stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n3.1 Registration\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When\r\nregistering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also\r\nregister via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years\r\nof age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account,\r\nthrough which you can rent vehicles.\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to\r\nkeep it up to date.\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in\r\nparticular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may\r\nonly be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use\r\nthe BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access\r\ndata. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using\r\nyour account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable\r\nfor any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use\r\nwas caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access\r\ndata by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided\r\nat the end of these ToS.\r\n3.2 Network Access and Device\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use\r\nthe Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your\r\nInternet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are\r\nresponsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile\r\nnetworks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the\r\ncontrol of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on\r\nall devices.\r\n3.3 Notifications\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text\r\nmessages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation.\r\nAdvertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n4. Single Vehicle Rental\r\n4.1 Rental Period\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle\r\nthrough the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental\r\nthe electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of\r\nthese ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time\r\nthe vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the\r\nextent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you\r\nrent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are\r\nresponsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are\r\nliable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as\r\nyour own responsibility.\r\n4.2 Availability; Maintenance\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ\r\nstrives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be\r\nadequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ\r\nguarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n4.3 Terms of Use\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree\r\nthat:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is\r\nlegally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes,\r\nand laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case\r\nmay be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists,\r\npedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are\r\nnot relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the\r\nrisk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any\r\nresulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation\r\nduring the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other\r\nreasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using\r\nthe Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of\r\nBRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a\r\nvehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject\r\nto additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the\r\nlocal police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving\r\nnot only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or\r\n\r\nstolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ\r\narising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n4.5 Checking the Vehicle\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front\r\nand rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these\r\nToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical\r\ndefect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness.\r\nBRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect\r\nthat may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to\r\nsection 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from\r\ndamage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of\r\nage, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental\r\ncondition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the\r\nability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol,\r\ndrugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate\r\nthe Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that\r\nmay distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or\r\nthunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s\r\nroadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are\r\nusing the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-\r\nroad trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a\r\nVehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be\r\nfreely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric\r\nScooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within\r\nthe boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the\r\nBRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List\r\n(hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you\r\ncan view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the\r\nBRIZ app.\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:10:33',	'2019-05-14 14:10:33',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(188,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:11:05',	'2019-05-14 14:11:05',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\nBRIZ App means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android\r\nand iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\nBRIZ Website means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\nBRIZ Rental Contract means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each\r\nSingle Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\nForce Majeure Event means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the\r\ncontrol of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods,\r\nearthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other\r\nelements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection,\r\nriots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-\r\nouts, and civil unrest.\r\nSingle Vehicle Rental means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the\r\nconfirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS.\r\nOther Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your\r\nauthorization.\r\n\r\nOperating Area means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally\r\nbe rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nRental Time means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in\r\naccordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental\r\nContract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\nServices means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles\r\ntogether with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in\r\nyour country of residence.\r\nSubscription means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a\r\ncertain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or\r\nannual pass subscription).\r\nToS means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each\r\nBRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nVehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n2. Contractual Object\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time\r\nto time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles\r\nmade available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may\r\nbe, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List\r\n(hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your\r\nlocation will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are\r\nand remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The\r\ncountries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n3. BRIZ App and Website; Account\r\nYou can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online\r\napplication stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n3.1 Registration\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When\r\nregistering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also\r\nregister via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years\r\nof age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account,\r\nthrough which you can rent vehicles.\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to\r\nkeep it up to date.\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in\r\nparticular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may\r\nonly be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use\r\nthe BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access\r\ndata. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using\r\nyour account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable\r\nfor any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use\r\nwas caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access\r\ndata by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided\r\nat the end of these ToS.\r\n3.2 Network Access and Device\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use\r\nthe Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your\r\nInternet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are\r\nresponsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile\r\nnetworks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the\r\ncontrol of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on\r\nall devices.\r\n3.3 Notifications\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text\r\nmessages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation.\r\nAdvertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n4. Single Vehicle Rental\r\n4.1 Rental Period\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle\r\nthrough the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental\r\nthe electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of\r\nthese ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time\r\nthe vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the\r\nextent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you\r\nrent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are\r\nresponsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are\r\nliable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as\r\nyour own responsibility.\r\n4.2 Availability; Maintenance\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ\r\nstrives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be\r\nadequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ\r\nguarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n4.3 Terms of Use\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree\r\nthat:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is\r\nlegally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes,\r\nand laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case\r\nmay be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists,\r\npedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are\r\nnot relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the\r\nrisk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any\r\nresulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation\r\nduring the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other\r\nreasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using\r\nthe Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of\r\nBRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a\r\nvehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject\r\nto additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the\r\nlocal police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving\r\nnot only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or\r\n\r\nstolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ\r\narising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n4.5 Checking the Vehicle\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front\r\nand rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these\r\nToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical\r\ndefect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness.\r\nBRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect\r\nthat may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to\r\nsection 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from\r\ndamage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of\r\nage, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental\r\ncondition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the\r\nability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol,\r\ndrugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate\r\nthe Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that\r\nmay distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or\r\nthunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s\r\nroadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are\r\nusing the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-\r\nroad trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a\r\nVehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be\r\nfreely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric\r\nScooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within\r\nthe boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the\r\nBRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List\r\n(hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you\r\ncan view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the\r\nBRIZ app.\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:11:05',	'2019-05-14 14:11:05',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(189,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:12:08',	'2019-05-14 14:12:08',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\nOperating Area means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally\r\nbe rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nRental Time means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in\r\naccordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental\r\nContract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\nServices means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles\r\ntogether with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in\r\nyour country of residence.\r\nSubscription means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a\r\ncertain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or\r\nannual pass subscription).\r\nToS means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each\r\nBRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nVehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n2. Contractual Object\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time\r\nto time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles\r\nmade available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may\r\nbe, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List\r\n(hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your\r\nlocation will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are\r\nand remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The\r\ncountries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n3. BRIZ App and Website; Account\r\nYou can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online\r\napplication stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n3.1 Registration\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When\r\nregistering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also\r\nregister via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years\r\nof age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account,\r\nthrough which you can rent vehicles.\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to\r\nkeep it up to date.\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in\r\nparticular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may\r\nonly be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use\r\nthe BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access\r\ndata. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using\r\nyour account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable\r\nfor any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use\r\nwas caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access\r\ndata by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided\r\nat the end of these ToS.\r\n3.2 Network Access and Device\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use\r\nthe Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your\r\nInternet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are\r\nresponsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile\r\nnetworks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the\r\ncontrol of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on\r\nall devices.\r\n3.3 Notifications\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text\r\nmessages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation.\r\nAdvertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n4. Single Vehicle Rental\r\n4.1 Rental Period\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle\r\nthrough the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental\r\nthe electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of\r\nthese ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time\r\nthe vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the\r\nextent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you\r\nrent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are\r\nresponsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are\r\nliable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as\r\nyour own responsibility.\r\n4.2 Availability; Maintenance\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ\r\nstrives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be\r\nadequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ\r\nguarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n4.3 Terms of Use\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree\r\nthat:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is\r\nlegally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes,\r\nand laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case\r\nmay be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists,\r\npedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are\r\nnot relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the\r\nrisk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any\r\nresulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation\r\nduring the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other\r\nreasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using\r\nthe Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of\r\nBRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a\r\nvehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject\r\nto additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the\r\nlocal police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving\r\nnot only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or\r\n\r\nstolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ\r\narising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n4.5 Checking the Vehicle\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front\r\nand rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these\r\nToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical\r\ndefect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness.\r\nBRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect\r\nthat may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to\r\nsection 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from\r\ndamage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of\r\nage, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental\r\ncondition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the\r\nability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol,\r\ndrugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate\r\nthe Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that\r\nmay distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or\r\nthunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s\r\nroadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are\r\nusing the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-\r\nroad trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a\r\nVehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be\r\nfreely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric\r\nScooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within\r\nthe boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the\r\nBRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List\r\n(hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you\r\ncan view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the\r\nBRIZ app.\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:12:08',	'2019-05-14 14:12:08',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(190,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:12:44',	'2019-05-14 14:12:44',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\nServices means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles\r\ntogether with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in\r\nyour country of residence.\r\nSubscription means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a\r\ncertain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or\r\nannual pass subscription).\r\nToS means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each\r\nBRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nVehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n2. Contractual Object\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time\r\nto time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles\r\nmade available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may\r\nbe, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List\r\n(hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your\r\nlocation will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are\r\nand remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The\r\ncountries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n3. BRIZ App and Website; Account\r\nYou can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online\r\napplication stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n3.1 Registration\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When\r\nregistering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also\r\nregister via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years\r\nof age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account,\r\nthrough which you can rent vehicles.\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to\r\nkeep it up to date.\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in\r\nparticular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may\r\nonly be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use\r\nthe BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access\r\ndata. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using\r\nyour account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable\r\nfor any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use\r\nwas caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access\r\ndata by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided\r\nat the end of these ToS.\r\n3.2 Network Access and Device\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use\r\nthe Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your\r\nInternet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are\r\nresponsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile\r\nnetworks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the\r\ncontrol of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on\r\nall devices.\r\n3.3 Notifications\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text\r\nmessages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation.\r\nAdvertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n4. Single Vehicle Rental\r\n4.1 Rental Period\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle\r\nthrough the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental\r\nthe electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of\r\nthese ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time\r\nthe vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the\r\nextent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you\r\nrent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are\r\nresponsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are\r\nliable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as\r\nyour own responsibility.\r\n4.2 Availability; Maintenance\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ\r\nstrives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be\r\nadequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ\r\nguarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n4.3 Terms of Use\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree\r\nthat:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is\r\nlegally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes,\r\nand laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case\r\nmay be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists,\r\npedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are\r\nnot relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the\r\nrisk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any\r\nresulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation\r\nduring the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other\r\nreasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using\r\nthe Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of\r\nBRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a\r\nvehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject\r\nto additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the\r\nlocal police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving\r\nnot only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or\r\n\r\nstolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ\r\narising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n4.5 Checking the Vehicle\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front\r\nand rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these\r\nToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical\r\ndefect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness.\r\nBRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect\r\nthat may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to\r\nsection 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from\r\ndamage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of\r\nage, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental\r\ncondition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the\r\nability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol,\r\ndrugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate\r\nthe Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that\r\nmay distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or\r\nthunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s\r\nroadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are\r\nusing the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-\r\nroad trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a\r\nVehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be\r\nfreely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric\r\nScooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within\r\nthe boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the\r\nBRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List\r\n(hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you\r\ncan view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the\r\nBRIZ app.\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:12:44',	'2019-05-14 14:12:44',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(191,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:13:34',	'2019-05-14 14:13:34',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time\r\nto time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles\r\nmade available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may\r\nbe, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List\r\n(hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your\r\nlocation will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are\r\nand remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The\r\ncountries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n3. BRIZ App and Website; Account\r\nYou can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online\r\napplication stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n3.1 Registration\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When\r\nregistering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also\r\nregister via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years\r\nof age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account,\r\nthrough which you can rent vehicles.\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to\r\nkeep it up to date.\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in\r\nparticular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may\r\nonly be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use\r\nthe BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access\r\ndata. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using\r\nyour account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable\r\nfor any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use\r\nwas caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access\r\ndata by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided\r\nat the end of these ToS.\r\n3.2 Network Access and Device\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use\r\nthe Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your\r\nInternet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are\r\nresponsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the\r\nBRIZ App.\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile\r\nnetworks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the\r\ncontrol of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on\r\nall devices.\r\n3.3 Notifications\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text\r\nmessages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation.\r\nAdvertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n4. Single Vehicle Rental\r\n4.1 Rental Period\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle\r\nthrough the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental\r\nthe electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of\r\nthese ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time\r\nthe vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the\r\nextent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you\r\nrent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are\r\nresponsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are\r\nliable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as\r\nyour own responsibility.\r\n4.2 Availability; Maintenance\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ\r\nstrives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be\r\nadequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ\r\nguarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n4.3 Terms of Use\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree\r\nthat:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is\r\nlegally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes,\r\nand laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case\r\nmay be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists,\r\npedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are\r\nnot relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the\r\nrisk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any\r\nresulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation\r\nduring the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other\r\nreasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using\r\nthe Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of\r\nBRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a\r\nvehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject\r\nto additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the\r\nlocal police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving\r\nnot only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or\r\n\r\nstolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ\r\narising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n4.5 Checking the Vehicle\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front\r\nand rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these\r\nToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical\r\ndefect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness.\r\nBRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect\r\nthat may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to\r\nsection 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from\r\ndamage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of\r\nage, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental\r\ncondition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the\r\nability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol,\r\ndrugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate\r\nthe Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that\r\nmay distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or\r\nthunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s\r\nroadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are\r\nusing the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-\r\nroad trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a\r\nVehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be\r\nfreely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric\r\nScooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within\r\nthe boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the\r\nBRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List\r\n(hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you\r\ncan view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the\r\nBRIZ app.\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:13:34',	'2019-05-14 14:13:34',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(192,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:20:29',	'2019-05-14 14:20:29',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ\r\nstrives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be\r\nadequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ\r\nguarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n4.3 Terms of Use\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree\r\nthat:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is\r\nlegally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes,\r\nand laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case\r\nmay be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists,\r\npedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are\r\nnot relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the\r\nrisk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any\r\nresulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation\r\nduring the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other\r\nreasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using\r\nthe Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of\r\nBRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a\r\nvehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject\r\nto additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the\r\nlocal police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving\r\nnot only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or\r\n\r\nstolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ\r\narising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n4.5 Checking the Vehicle\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front\r\nand rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these\r\nToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical\r\ndefect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness.\r\nBRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect\r\nthat may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to\r\nsection 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from\r\ndamage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of\r\nage, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental\r\ncondition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the\r\nability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol,\r\ndrugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate\r\nthe Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that\r\nmay distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or\r\nthunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s\r\nroadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are\r\nusing the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-\r\nroad trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a\r\nVehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be\r\nfreely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric\r\nScooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within\r\nthe boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the\r\nBRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List\r\n(hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you\r\ncan view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the\r\nBRIZ app.\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:20:29',	'2019-05-14 14:20:29',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(193,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:23:22',	'2019-05-14 14:23:22',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the\r\nlocal police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving\r\nnot only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or\r\n\r\nstolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ\r\narising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n4.5 Checking the Vehicle\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front\r\nand rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these\r\nToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical\r\ndefect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness.\r\nBRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect\r\nthat may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to\r\nsection 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from\r\ndamage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of\r\nage, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental\r\ncondition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the\r\nability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol,\r\ndrugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate\r\nthe Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that\r\nmay distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or\r\nthunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s\r\nroadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are\r\nusing the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-\r\nroad trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a\r\nVehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be\r\nfreely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric\r\nScooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within\r\nthe boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the\r\nBRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List\r\n(hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you\r\ncan view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the\r\nBRIZ app.\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:23:22',	'2019-05-14 14:23:22',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(194,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:25:47',	'2019-05-14 14:25:47',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:25:47',	'2019-05-14 14:25:47',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(195,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:26:01',	'2019-05-14 14:26:01',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n4.6 Prohibited Use\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:26:01',	'2019-05-14 14:26:01',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(196,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:26:12',	'2019-05-14 14:26:12',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.6 Prohibited Use</strong>\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet\r\nconnection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the\r\ncontact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ\r\nRental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental\r\nContracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of\r\nthe BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ\r\nwith information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific\r\nconditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other\r\nroad or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at\r\ntrees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property\r\nof third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire\r\ndepartment service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access\r\npaths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian\r\ncrossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle\r\ncovers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered\r\nitem is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the\r\nareas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and,\r\nin general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are\r\ndriving the Vehicle.\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related\r\nholding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are\r\nalso not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than\r\n24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00\r\no&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the\r\naffected area.\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you\r\nfor any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if\r\nthe Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will\r\ncontinue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions,\r\nbut no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The\r\ncorresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are\r\nnot responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the\r\ndamage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:26:12',	'2019-05-14 14:26:12',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(197,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:28:00',	'2019-05-14 14:28:00',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.6 Prohibited Use</strong>\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet connection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the contact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ Rental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ with information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific conditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other road or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at trees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property of third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire department service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access paths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian crossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle covers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered item is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the areas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and, in general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are driving the Vehicle.\r\n\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related holding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are also not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the affected area.\r\n\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you for any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if the Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will continue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions, but no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The corresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are not responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the damage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n\r\n<strong>6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing</strong>\r\n\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price\r\nList (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\nIn addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins.\r\nBRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in\r\naccordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to\r\nthe current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as\r\nindicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\nPayments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract\r\nmonth or contract year.\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you\r\nmay charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as\r\nyour preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit\r\ncard (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses\r\nthe _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information\r\nsee section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you\r\nwill be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to\r\nconfirm.\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account,\r\nthe Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other\r\npayments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion\r\nprovide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately\r\nby BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your\r\nCredit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a\r\nbalance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and\r\ninsofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the\r\namounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the\r\n(remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ\r\nApp or any other third party.\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event\r\nof termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a\r\ndesignated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any\r\nremaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor\r\nmay these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by\r\nlaw (e.g. value added tax).\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the\r\napplicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove\r\nthat no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet\r\nyour payment obligations.\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit\r\nAccount and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such\r\nrecoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n7. Term and Termination\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:28:00',	'2019-05-14 14:28:00',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(198,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:30:07',	'2019-05-14 14:30:07',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.6 Prohibited Use</strong>\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet connection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the contact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ Rental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ with information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific conditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other road or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at trees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property of third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire department service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access paths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian crossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle covers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered item is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the areas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and, in general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are driving the Vehicle.\r\n\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related holding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are also not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the affected area.\r\n\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you for any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if the Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will continue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions, but no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The corresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are not responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the damage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n\r\n<strong>6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing</strong>\r\n\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App. In addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins. BRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in accordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to the current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as indicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract. Payments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract month or contract year.\r\n\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you may charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as your preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit card (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses the _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information see section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you will be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to confirm.\r\n\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account, the Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other payments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion provide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately by BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your Credit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a balance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and insofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the amounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the (remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ App or any other third party.\r\n\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event of termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a designated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any remaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor may these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by law (e.g. value added tax).\r\n\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the applicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove that no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet your payment obligations.\r\n\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such recoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n\r\n<strong>7. Term and Termination</strong>\r\n\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by\r\ngiving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle\r\nRental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App\r\nnotification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a\r\ntermination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees\r\nwithin 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you\r\ncommunicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to\r\nsection 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in\r\naccordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right\r\nThe extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1\r\nand 7.2 of these ToS\r\n8. Liability and Limitation of Liability\r\n8.1 Your Liability\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to\r\ntheft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of\r\nslight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric\r\nScooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of\r\nthese ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the\r\nPrice List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment\r\nhas occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ\r\nreserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and\r\nagents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses\r\narising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS,\r\n(ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to\r\nOther Drivers.\r\n8.2 BRIZ’s Liability\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:30:07',	'2019-05-14 14:30:07',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(199,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:32:07',	'2019-05-14 14:32:07',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.6 Prohibited Use</strong>\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet connection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the contact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ Rental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ with information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific conditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other road or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at trees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property of third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire department service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access paths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian crossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle covers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered item is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the areas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and, in general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are driving the Vehicle.\r\n\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related holding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are also not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the affected area.\r\n\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you for any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if the Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will continue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions, but no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The corresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are not responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the damage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n\r\n<strong>6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing</strong>\r\n\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App. In addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins. BRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in accordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to the current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as indicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract. Payments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract month or contract year.\r\n\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you may charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as your preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit card (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses the _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information see section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you will be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to confirm.\r\n\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account, the Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other payments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion provide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately by BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your Credit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a balance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and insofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the amounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the (remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ App or any other third party.\r\n\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event of termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a designated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any remaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor may these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by law (e.g. value added tax).\r\n\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the applicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove that no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet your payment obligations.\r\n\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such recoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n\r\n<strong>7. Term and Termination</strong>\r\n\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle Rental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App notification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a termination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees within 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you communicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to section 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in accordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right The extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1 and 7.2 of these ToS\r\n\r\n<strong>8. Liability and Limitation of Liability</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>8.1 Your Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to theft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of slight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric Scooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of these ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the Price List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment has occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ reserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and agents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses arising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS, (ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to Other Drivers.\r\n\r\n<strong>8.2 BRIZ’s Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties\r\n(“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal\r\nObligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the\r\ncontractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper\r\n\r\nperformance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and\r\ntrust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not\r\nresult in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of\r\nthe typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages\r\nresulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious\r\nagents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is\r\nexcluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3.\r\nBRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of\r\nforce majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the\r\ncustomer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions,\r\nthis shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and\r\nvicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n9. Privacy Notice\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:32:07',	'2019-05-14 14:32:07',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(200,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:33:16',	'2019-05-14 14:33:16',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.6 Prohibited Use</strong>\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet connection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the contact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ Rental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ with information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific conditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other road or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at trees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property of third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire department service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access paths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian crossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle covers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered item is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the areas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and, in general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are driving the Vehicle.\r\n\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related holding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are also not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the affected area.\r\n\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you for any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if the Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will continue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions, but no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The corresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are not responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the damage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n\r\n<strong>6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing</strong>\r\n\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App. In addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins. BRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in accordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to the current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as indicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract. Payments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract month or contract year.\r\n\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you may charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as your preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit card (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses the _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information see section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you will be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to confirm.\r\n\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account, the Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other payments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion provide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately by BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your Credit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a balance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and insofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the amounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the (remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ App or any other third party.\r\n\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event of termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a designated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any remaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor may these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by law (e.g. value added tax).\r\n\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the applicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove that no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet your payment obligations.\r\n\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such recoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n\r\n<strong>7. Term and Termination</strong>\r\n\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle Rental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App notification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a termination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees within 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you communicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to section 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in accordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right The extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1 and 7.2 of these ToS\r\n\r\n<strong>8. Liability and Limitation of Liability</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>8.1 Your Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to theft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of slight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric Scooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of these ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the Price List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment has occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ reserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and agents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses arising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS, (ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to Other Drivers.\r\n\r\n<strong>8.2 BRIZ’s Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties (“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal Obligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the contractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper performance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and trust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not result in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of the typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages resulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious agents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is excluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3. BRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of force majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the customer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions, this shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>9. Privacy Notice</strong>\r\n\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n11. Content of Third Parties\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or\r\nsponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third\r\nparty services.\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the\r\nBRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n12. Applicable Law\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the\r\nlaws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n13. Transfer\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third\r\nparty at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time\r\nbefore such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to\r\nterminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to\r\nthird parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n14. No Waiver\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these\r\nToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these\r\nToS.\r\n15. Validity\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared\r\ninvalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or\r\nPrice List (hyperlink).\r\n16. Remark of Dispute\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a\r\nFederal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution\r\nPlatform\r\nhttps://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage on\r\nalternative dispute resolution.\r\n17. Customer Service\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through\r\nthe BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-\r\nmail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:33:16',	'2019-05-14 14:33:16',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(201,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:35:28',	'2019-05-14 14:35:28',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.6 Prohibited Use</strong>\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet connection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the contact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ Rental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ with information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific conditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other road or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at trees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property of third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire department service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access paths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian crossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle covers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered item is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the areas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and, in general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are driving the Vehicle.\r\n\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related holding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are also not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the affected area.\r\n\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you for any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if the Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will continue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions, but no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The corresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are not responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the damage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n\r\n<strong>6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing</strong>\r\n\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App. In addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins. BRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in accordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to the current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as indicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract. Payments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract month or contract year.\r\n\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you may charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as your preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit card (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses the _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information see section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you will be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to confirm.\r\n\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account, the Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other payments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion provide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately by BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your Credit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a balance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and insofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the amounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the (remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ App or any other third party.\r\n\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event of termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a designated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any remaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor may these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by law (e.g. value added tax).\r\n\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the applicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove that no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet your payment obligations.\r\n\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such recoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n\r\n<strong>7. Term and Termination</strong>\r\n\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle Rental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App notification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a termination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees within 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you communicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to section 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in accordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right The extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1 and 7.2 of these ToS\r\n\r\n<strong>8. Liability and Limitation of Liability</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>8.1 Your Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to theft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of slight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric Scooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of these ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the Price List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment has occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ reserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and agents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses arising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS, (ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to Other Drivers.\r\n\r\n<strong>8.2 BRIZ’s Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties (“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal Obligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the contractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper performance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and trust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not result in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of the typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages resulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious agents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is excluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3. BRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of force majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the customer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions, this shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>9. Privacy Notice</strong>\r\n\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n10. Changes to these ToS and Prices\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in\r\naccordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without\r\ngiving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at\r\nleast three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions\r\nthat (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will\r\nremain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify\r\nyou of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month.\r\nAll notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week\r\nafter communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the\r\nSubscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the\r\naforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of\r\nany such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified\r\nchanges are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after\r\ncommunication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription\r\nwill automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned\r\nconsequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price\r\nList (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a\r\nchange in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with\r\neffect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do\r\nnot object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will\r\nparticularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If\r\nmandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above\r\ndeadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the\r\ncurrent contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force.\r\nHowever, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual\r\nSubscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three\r\ndays.\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or\r\nnotification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the\r\nBRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List\r\n(hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also\r\napplies to this text form requirement.\r\n\r\n<strong>11. Content of Third Parties</strong>\r\n\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or sponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third party services.\r\n\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the BRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n\r\n<strong>12. Applicable Law</strong>\r\n\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the laws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n<strong>13. Transfer</strong>\r\n\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third party at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time before such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to third parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>14. No Waiver</strong>\r\n\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these ToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>15. Validity</strong>\r\n\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared invalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>16. Remark of Dispute</strong>\r\n\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a Federal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution Platform <a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage\">https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage</a> on alternative dispute resolution.\r\n\r\n<strong>17. Customer Service</strong>\r\n\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through the BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-mail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:35:28',	'2019-05-14 14:35:28',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(202,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:36:59',	'2019-05-14 14:36:59',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.6 Prohibited Use</strong>\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet connection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the contact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ Rental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ with information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific conditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other road or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at trees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property of third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire department service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access paths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian crossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle covers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered item is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the areas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and, in general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are driving the Vehicle.\r\n\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related holding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are also not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the affected area.\r\n\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you for any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if the Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will continue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions, but no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The corresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are not responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the damage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n\r\n<strong>6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing</strong>\r\n\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App. In addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins. BRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in accordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to the current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as indicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract. Payments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract month or contract year.\r\n\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you may charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as your preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit card (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses the _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information see section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you will be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to confirm.\r\n\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account, the Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other payments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion provide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately by BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your Credit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a balance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and insofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the amounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the (remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ App or any other third party.\r\n\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event of termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a designated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any remaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor may these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by law (e.g. value added tax).\r\n\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the applicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove that no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet your payment obligations.\r\n\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such recoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n\r\n<strong>7. Term and Termination</strong>\r\n\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle Rental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App notification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a termination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees within 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you communicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to section 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in accordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right The extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1 and 7.2 of these ToS\r\n\r\n<strong>8. Liability and Limitation of Liability</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>8.1 Your Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to theft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of slight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric Scooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of these ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the Price List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment has occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ reserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and agents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses arising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS, (ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to Other Drivers.\r\n\r\n<strong>8.2 BRIZ’s Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties (“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal Obligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the contractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper performance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and trust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not result in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of the typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages resulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious agents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is excluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3. BRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of force majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the customer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions, this shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>9. Privacy Notice</strong>\r\n\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration\r\nand use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details\r\nas well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of\r\ndeparture, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in\r\ncompliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection\r\nRegulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is\r\nbased on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to\r\nidentify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules\r\nand to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit\r\ncard, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered\r\nin England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license\r\nNr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose\r\npayment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter\r\nwill be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit\r\ncard transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here:\r\nhttps://payally.eu/privacy-policy. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the\r\nbasis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your\r\npersonal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our\r\nPrivacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your\r\npersonal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>10. Changes to these ToS and Prices</strong>\r\n\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in accordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without giving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at least three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions that (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will remain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month. All notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned consequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a change in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with effect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do not object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will particularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If mandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above deadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the current contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force. However, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual Subscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three days.\r\n\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or notification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also applies to this text form requirement.\r\n\r\n<strong>11. Content of Third Parties</strong>\r\n\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or sponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third party services.\r\n\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the BRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n\r\n<strong>12. Applicable Law</strong>\r\n\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the laws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n<strong>13. Transfer</strong>\r\n\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third party at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time before such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to third parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>14. No Waiver</strong>\r\n\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these ToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>15. Validity</strong>\r\n\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared invalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>16. Remark of Dispute</strong>\r\n\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a Federal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution Platform <a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage\">https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage</a> on alternative dispute resolution.\r\n\r\n<strong>17. Customer Service</strong>\r\n\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through the BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-mail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:36:59',	'2019-05-14 14:36:59',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(203,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:38:20',	'2019-05-14 14:38:20',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\r\n\r\n<strong>Content\r\n</strong>\r\n1. These Terms of Service (“ToS”) regulate the business relationship between BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (“we”, “us”, “our”, “BRIZ”) and natural persons who want to use our Electric Scooters in Switzerland (“you”, “your”).\r\n\r\n2. These ToS and the respective Price List (hyperlink) shall apply to the BRIZ Rental Contract concluded when you register a BRIZ user account, to each purchase of a Subscription or to each Single Vehicle Rental during your BRIZ journey. By accepting these ToS you agree to be bound by its terms and the current Price List (“Price List”) (hyperlink) as amended from time to time.\r\n\r\n3. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in Switzerland, the French or German text of these ToS shall prevail. The English version is for information purposes only. Customers who wish to rent out vehicles in other countries, the respective text of the ToS of that country is the legally binding version.\r\n\r\n<strong>1. Definitions</strong>\r\n\r\n<em>Terms in capital letters used in these ToS have the meaning assigned to them in these ToS.</em>\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter means</strong> the electric scooter made available by BRIZ for rent that is equipped with or consists of a board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and IoT module with GPS device in it.\r\n\r\n<strong>Electric Scooter Rental</strong> means the rental of an Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App. BRIZ Account means a personal account provided to you by BRIZ after a successful registration.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ App</strong> means the software application developed by BRIZ which operates on Android and iOS operational systems enabling Electric Scooter Rental and return of Vehicles.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Website</strong> means the official website of BRIZ, accessible under http://www.briz.app/.\r\n\r\n<strong>BRIZ Rental Contract</strong> means the contract that is concluded between you and BRIZ for each Single Vehicle Rental or Subscription.\r\n\r\n<strong>Force Majeure Event</strong> means the occurrence of any event or circumstance beyond the control of BRIZ. Force Majeure Events include (i) natural disasters, explosions, fires, floods, earthquakes, epidemics, catastrophic weather conditions, atmospheric disasters or other elements of nature, (ii) acts of war (declared or undeclared), acts of terrorism, insurrection, riots, rebellion, sabotage, (iii) exceptional traffic and road situations and (iv) strikes, lock-outs, and civil unrest.\r\n\r\n<strong>Single Vehicle Rental</strong> means each individual rental of Electric Scooter beginning with the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS. Other Driver means any person using a Vehicle you rented on your account with your authorization.\r\n\r\n<strong>Operating Area</strong> means the Area within the boundaries of which the Vehicles can generally be rented and returned. The Operating Area can be viewed, on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>Rental Time</strong> means the period of time between the confirmation of the booking in accordance with section 4.1 paragraph (1) of these ToS and the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract in accordance with section 5 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>Services</strong> means the entirety of services offered by BRIZ including rental of Vehicles together with the provision of the BRIZ App all as described in these ToS, as available in your country of residence.\r\n\r\n<strong>Subscription</strong> means the continuous subscription for purchase within the App, including a certain number of time-limited vehicle rentals within a certain time period (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription).\r\n\r\n<strong>ToS</strong> means these terms of service including the Price List (hyperlink) that apply to each BRIZ Rental Contract. Vehicle(s) means Electric Scooters or potentially another device, made available by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>2. Contractual Object</strong>\r\n\r\n2.1 Subject to the terms of these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), as amended from time to time (see section 10 of these ToS), BRIZ offers the possibility to rent and use Vehicles made available by BRIZ in the Operating Area on a pay per ride basis and, as the case may be, under a one-day or under a subscription as indicated in the BRIZ App and Price List (hyperlink), subject to availability. Locations and categories of Vehicles available at your location will be displayed in the BRIZ App. The Vehicles and all rights to the Services are and remain the exclusive property of BRIZ at all times.\r\n\r\n2.2 Electric Scooters are currently not offered in all countries in which BRIZ operates. The countries where Electronic Scooters are offered are from the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n<strong>3. BRIZ App and Website</strong>\r\n\r\nAccount You can rent available Vehicles via the BRIZ App which can be downloaded from online application stores or the BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.1 Registration</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Before you can rent our Vehicles, you must register a BRIZ Account via BRIZ App. When registering, you must provide your phone number to BRIZ. Alternatively, you can also register via your Facebook or Google account. To create an account, you must be 18 years of age or older. After successful registration, you will gain access to your BRIZ Account, through which you can rent vehicles.\r\n\r\nB. Setting up a BRIZ Account is free.\r\n\r\nC. You are obliged to provide truthful and complete information during registration and to keep it up to date.\r\n\r\nD. You are obliged to inform BRIZ immediately of changes to your personal data, in particular regarding your billing information.\r\n\r\nE. Your access data (username, password) for the BRIZ Account are individualised and may only be used by you. You may not grant third parties access to your BRIZ Account or use the BRIZ Account of a third party. You are responsible for the confidentiality of your access data. BRIZ is not liable for any loss that you may incur as a result of someone else using your account, except if such use was caused willfully or negligently by BRIZ. You are liable for any loss or damage resulting from the use of your account by third parties if such use was caused by you intentionally or negligently. In case of suspected misuse of your access data by a third party, you must notify BRIZ immediately under the contact details as provided at the end of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.2 Network Access and Device</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You are responsible for the network connections on your device that are required to use the Services and for any access or data fees incurred from third parties (such as your Internet provider or mobile carrier) in connection with your use of Our Services. You are responsible for acquiring and updating network-enabled (mobile) devices needed to use the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nB. You acknowledge that BRIZ´s Services are provided over the Internet and mobile networks, the quality and availability of the Services may be affected by factors beyond the control of BRIZ. BRIZ makes no warranty that the Services or any part thereof will work on all devices.\r\n\r\n<strong>3.3 Notifications</strong>\r\n\r\nBy setting up a BRIZ Account, you agree that BRIZ may send you informational text messages (SMS), emails, and push notifications as part of the normal business operation. Advertising will only be sent to you if you has expressly consented to it.\r\n\r\n<strong>4. Single Vehicle Rental</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>4.1 Rental Period</strong>\r\n\r\nA. The Single Vehicle Rental will commence once you indicate your desire to rent a Vehicle through the BRIZ App and BRIZ confirmed the rental, in case of an Electric Scooter Rental the electric power of the Electric Scooter, shall be activated.\r\n\r\nB. The Single Vehicle Rental ends once a Vehicle is returned in accordance with section 5 of these ToS or if BRIZ terminates the Single Vehicle Rental in accordance with these ToS.\r\n\r\nC. During the Rental Time, you are responsible for the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nD. You must not leave a Vehicle unattended at any time during the Rental Time. Each time the vehicles are parked, use the kickstand on the Vehicle.\r\n\r\nE. In principle, you may only rent one Vehicle at a time on your BRIZ Account. If and to the extent this is expressly offered via BRIZ App, you may rent a few Vehicles at a time. If you rent more than one Vehicle and leave one or more Vehicles to Other Drivers, you are responsible to inform such Other Drivers of all obligations arising from these ToS. You are liable to Vehicles for the actions of Other Drivers to whom you assign a Vehicle for use, as your own responsibility.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.2 Availability; Maintenance</strong>\r\n\r\nA. Vehicles are rented subject to availability on a first come, first-serve basis. Although BRIZ strives to meet the demand for the Vehicles, BRIZ cannot guarantee that supply will be adequate to provide a Vehicle to every customer at any time.\r\n\r\nB. BRIZ is responsible for the daily maintenance and repair of the Vehicles. However, BRIZ guarantee that all Vehicles available are in a trouble-free condition at any time.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.3 Terms of Use</strong>\r\n\r\nA. As a precedent condition for each BRIZ Rental Contract, you acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you are experienced and familiar with the safe handling of the selected vehicle;\r\nb) you are physically and mentally fit to ride the Vehicle you chose;\r\nc) you are required to wear a helmet if the rental area in which you rent the vehicle is legally compulsory or imported;\r\nd) you are familiar with all applicable local, state, and county rules, regulations, codes, and laws that relate to the safe and legal operation of an electric scooter as the case may be.\r\ne) you are aware that riding an electric scooter on the road due to motorists, pedestrians and road conditions can present an accident risk and you must drive\r\ncarefully to avoid such accidents;\r\nf) you are in a position to operate and drive the selected Vehicle properly, and you are not relying on BRIZ to explain to you how to operate or ride such Vehicle;\r\ng) you are aware that the use of a helmet and/or protective clothing cannot preclude the risk of personal injury in the event of an accident.\r\n\r\nB. You further acknowledge and agree that:\r\na) you undertake to comply with the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG);\r\nb) you are responsible for the procurement of a helmet and/or other protective clothing;\r\nc) you are responsible for the quality and correct use of the protective clothing you use;\r\nd) you are responsible for treating the chosen Vehicle with care and professionalism;\r\ne) you are liable during the rental period for traffic violations committed by you and any resulting costs and fees, including any fees for improper parking of the vehicles;\r\nf) BRIZ reserves the right to identify you to Authorities if you commit a traffic violation during the rental period or if BRIZ is required by law to provide information for other reasons;\r\ng) BRIZ is under no obligation to take out insurance in your favour;\r\nh) you will be solely responsible for any damage caused to another person while using the Vehicle unless such damage was caused by an intentional or negligent act of BRIZ;\r\ni) you are obliged to adapt your driving behaviour to the weather conditions at all times;\r\nj) you are not allowed to remove or modify any accessories, parts or components of a vehicle;\r\nk) you may not use a Vehicle without intention to pay the charges;\r\nl) you may return the Vehicle outside the Operating Area as shown in the App, subject to additional fees in accordance with the Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>4.4 Obligation in the Event of an Accident</strong>\r\n\r\nYou must notify BRIZ under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS and the local police immediately if (i) an accident occurs during your rental of the Vehicle involving not only you but also third-parties and/or their property, or (ii) if a Vehicle is damaged or stolen during Rental Time by third parties. You are liable for any damages incurred by BRIZ arising from the culpable violation of this obligation.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.5 Checking the Vehicle</strong>\r\n\r\nA. You must inspect the Vehicle for any visible defects before the start of the journey;\r\nB. In particular, test the Electric Scooter’s operation components (board, a handle, a front and rear light, brakes, tires and a GPS device);\r\nC. You are obliged to notify the BRIZ (under the contact details provided at the end of these ToS) if during the rental period you determine that the selected Vehicle has a technical defect or malfunction that could obviously affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s driving or roadworthiness. BRIZ will cancel the BRIZ Rental Contract free of charge if you inform BRIZ about a defect that may affect a Vehicle´s roadworthiness within the first ten minutes after rental. Subject to section 8.2 paragraph 2 (BRIZ´s LIABILITY), the Vehicle shall be deemed to be free from damage if you do not notify BRIZ of any apparent defect within the first ten minutes after the\r\nrental date.\r\n\r\n<strong>4.6 Prohibited Use</strong>\r\n\r\nThe vehicles must not be used:\r\na) If the person who is supposed to ride the Electric Scooter is younger than 18 years of age, unless this person is accompanied by an adult;\r\nb) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle has any existing physical or mental condition that would prevent such person from safely operating the Vehicle;\r\nc) To carry objects which because of their shape, size or weight are likely to affect the ability of the driver to operate the Vehicle safely or to damage the Vehicle;\r\nd) If the person who is supposed to ride the Vehicle is under the influence of alcohol, drugs, or any other substance that may impair the person&amp;#39;s ability to safely operate the Vehicle;\r\ne) During the use and/or operation of mobile phones or other electronic devices that may distract the driver from the safe operation of the Vehicle;\r\nf) In adverse weather conditions like hail, dust storms, heavy fog, heavy rains, or thunderstorms;\r\ng) If the Vehicle has a manifest technical defect that could affect the Vehicle&amp;#39;s roadworthiness and the safety of the traffic;\r\nh) For violating the regulations of the Swiss Federal Road Traffic Act (SVG), if you are using the Services in Switzerland.\r\ni) For races, jumps, stunts, tricks riding, obstacle courses or similar uses and/or off-road trips;\r\nj) For any commercial purposes;\r\nk) For the purpose of towing, pulling, carrying, or pushing any person or object with a Vehicle;\r\nl) For the purpose of committing crimes.\r\n\r\n<strong>5. Return of a Vehicle and Termination of Single Rentals</strong>\r\n\r\n5.1 You must return the Vehicle in the same condition as when received. Vehicles must be freely accessible to third parties after a return.\r\n\r\n5.2 The rental period ends in the event of an Electric Scooter Rental (i) when the Electric Scooter is properly parked and locked at any legal, freely accessible parking location within the boundaries of the Operating Area, (ii) you have indicated the end of the rental via the BRIZ App and (iii) BRIZ confirms the return of the Electric Scooter via the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\nVehicles can be charged for an additional fee according to the applicable Price List (hyperlink) returned outside the Operating Area. After a successful return of a Vehicle, you can view the rental process including the entire rental period and the costs incurred in the BRIZ app.\r\n\r\n5.3 If the return of a Vehicle fails, eg due to a weak battery of your device or missing internet connection, you must notify the BRIZ as soon as possible via the BRIZ App or via the contact details provided at the end of these ToS. In such a case BRIZ closes the BRIZ Rental Contract manually. In addition, BRIZ reserves the right to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contracts if you do not use a Vehicle within a period of 24 hours after the commencement of the BRIZ Rental Contract.\r\n\r\n5.4 For a period of 24 hours after the return of a Vehicle, you must be able to provide BRIZ with information about the exact location of a returned Vehicle upon request.\r\n\r\n5.5 When parking a vehicle you are obliged to follow road traffic regulations and specific conditions of the Operating Area. You must make sure that the Vehicle does not hinder other road or sidewalk users or other third parties. In particular, you must not park the Vehicle at trees, traffic signs, traffic lights, parking meters, parking ticket machines, fences to property of third parties, benches, containers, litter bins, in front of or near emergency exits and fire department service zones, in front of driveways and exits, lowered curbstones, on access paths to public transportation, bicycle lanes, orientation aids for the blind, pedestrian crossings, in buildings, backyards, vehicles, parks and green spaces or where the Vehicle covers advertisements, urban furniture when the destination or functionality of the covered item is impaired or when the Vehicle damages or deteriorates the item´s condition, in the areas reserved for loading and unloading, in places reserved for other users or services and, in general, in any other places forbidden by local regulations of the city in which you are driving the Vehicle.\r\n\r\n5.6 You may not park the Vehicles on areas for which temporary, daily or time-related holding or parking bans exist (e.g. due to upcoming markets, parties, filming, etc.). You are also not permitted to park a vehicle on an area that is being stopped or parked in less than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked. For example, if such a ban begins at 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock one day, the Vehicle must not be parked after 09.00 o&amp;#39;clock the day before in the affected area.\r\n\r\n5.7 If you park the Vehicle in violation of the aforementioned provisions, we will charge you for any resulting costs in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), In addition, if the Vehicle is parked in violation of the provisions of Section 5.2, the rental period will continue to be chargeable until the Vehicle is returned in accordance with these provisions, but no later than 24 hours after the Vehicle has been parked in breach of these ToS. The corresponding fees will not be charged if and to the extent that you can prove that you are not responsible for the damage claimed by BRIZ, that no damage has occurred or that the damage actually incurred is lower than the costs charged to you.\r\n\r\n<strong>6. Payment; Invoicing and Balancing</strong>\r\n\r\n6.1 You agree to pay the prices of the chosen tariff in accordance with the applicable Price List (hyperlink), The valid price list can be viewed on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App. In addition, the applicable tariff for the single rent will be displayed before the rental begins. BRIZ is entitled to amend the Price List (hyperlink) at any time for future bookings in accordance with section 10 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n6.2 If a Vehicle is returned outside the Operating Area, additional fees are due according to the current Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n6.3 Different rates may apply to different categories of Electric Scooters or Vehicles as indicated in the BRIZ App or BRIZ Website.\r\n\r\n6.4 Fees for a BRIZ Rental Contract are due at the end of the BRIZ Rental Contract. Payments for Subscriptions (Monthly or Yearly) are due at the beginning of each contract month or contract year.\r\n\r\n6.5 After Registration, BRIZ sets up a credit account (“Credit Account”) for you, which you may charge with money at any time. You can choose between different payment methods as your preferred (“Preferred Payment Method”). So you can pay the amounts due by credit card (Visa, Mastercard or Maestro) or with PayPal. For payment by Credit Card BRIZ uses the _______ and for payments with PayPal, BRIZ uses the PayPal Sdk (for more information see section 9 of these ToS). If you deposit PayPal as your preferred payment method, you will be prompted to log in to your PayPal account using your email address and password to confirm.\r\n\r\n6.6 If and to the extent you have a credit balance (“Credit Balance”) on your Credit Account, the Credit Account for all due payments and then the Preferred Payment Method for all other payments due will be debited first. BRIZ may from time to time and at its own discretion provide you with bonus amounts (“Bonus Amounts”). Bonus amounts are listed separately by BRIZ within the BRIZ App (&amp;quot;Bonus Account&amp;quot;). You can view the total balance of your Credit and/or Bonus Account at any time in the BRIZ App. If and to the extent you have a balance on your Bonus Account, BRIZ will use first and foremost such balance. If and insofar as you have bonus amounts, BRIZ will first debit the Bonus Account with the amounts due. If there is no or insufficient credit on the Bonus Account, BRIZ will deduct the (remaining) amounts from your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method.\r\n\r\n6.7 You may not transfer your Bonus Amount or Credit Balance to other users of the BRIZ App or any other third party.\r\n\r\n6.8 There is no expiry date for your Credit Balance during the term of your use. In the event of termination, any Credit Amounts existing shall upon your request be transferred to a designated bank account as set out in section 7.1 paragraph (5) of these ToS. Any remaining bonus amounts will automatically be forfeited and will not be refunded to you, nor may these amounts be used to pay any payments owed to you by BRIZ.\r\n\r\n6.9 All costs stated in the Price List (hyperlink) are inclusive of applicable taxes required by law (e.g. value added tax).\r\n\r\n6.10 Should a due payment fail for reasons for which you are responsible, you owe BRIZ the applicable costs in accordance with the relevant Price List (hyperlink) unless you can prove that no costs have arisen or the actual costs incurred are lower than BRIZ asserted.\r\n\r\n6.11 In the event of late payment, BRIZ is entitled to discontinue the services until you meet your payment obligations.\r\n\r\n6.12 BRIZ automatically deducts all amounts due from your Bonus Account, your Credit Account and/or your Preferred Payment Method without prior notice. Objections to such recoveries must be made to BRIZ within 14 days of collection in writing (e.g. by e-mail).\r\n\r\n<strong>7. Term and Termination</strong>\r\n\r\n7.1 Term and Termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract\r\n\r\nA. The BRIZ Rental Contract concluded for an indefinite period.\r\nB. The monthly pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nC. The annual pass Subscription can be cancelled by you at any time without notice by giving notice in writing (e.g. e-mail or BRIZ App).\r\nD. It is not possible to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract before the end of a Single Vehicle Rental or a Subscription.\r\nE. Notice of termination from BRIZ must be given in text form (e.g. by email, SMS or by App notification). you may cancel a Subscription directly in the App or by sending us a termination notice in text form (e.g. via email).\r\nF. Upon termination of the BRIZ Rental Contract, BRIZ will collect any outstanding fees within 14 working days and then reimburse you any balance of your credit, provided you communicate the data of a due bank account to BRIZ via the contact details pursuant to section 17 of these ToS.\r\nG. You can terminate a BRIZ Rental Contract at any time by returning the Vehicle in accordance with section 5.2 of these ToS.\r\n\r\n7.2 Extraordinary Termination Right The extraordinary right of termination of the parties shall remain unaffected by sections 7.1 and 7.2 of these ToS\r\n\r\n<strong>8. Liability and Limitation of Liability</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>8.1 Your Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. In principle, you are liable for damage to a Vehicle or for damage caused by BRIZ due to theft or loss of a Vehicle in accordance with the statutory provisions. Your liability in case of slight negligence is limited to a maximum amount of CHF 450 for damages to an Electric Scooter.\r\nB. For damage caused by BRIZ due to a breach of these ToS, in particular to section 5 of these ToS, you are also liable according to the statutory provisions. If and as far as in the Price List (hyperlink). In each case, you are entitled to prove that no damage or impairment has occurred at all or is significantly lower than the flat rate. On the other hand, BRIZ reserves the right to determine that higher damage has occurred.\r\nC. You are obligated to indemnify, and hold BRIZ, its officers, directors, employees, and agents, harmless from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses arising out of or in any way connected with (i) your willful or negligent violation of these ToS, (ii) your willful or negligent violation of third party rights, or (iii) your leaving of Vehicles to Other Drivers.\r\n\r\n<strong>8.2 BRIZ’s Liability</strong>\r\n\r\nA. BRIZ is fully liable to you in the event of a culpable breach of material contractual duties (“Cardinal Obligations”) by BRIZ, BRIZ’s legal representatives or vicarious agents. Cardinal Obligations are all obligations whose breach would jeopardize the achievement of the contractual purpose, as well as all obligations whose fulfilment enables the proper performance of the agreement in the first place and on which you can generally rely and trust. If the breach of a Cardinal Obligation is due only to slight negligence and does not result in injury to life, limb or health, your claims will be limited to damages in the amount of the typically foreseeable damage at the time the service provided.\r\nB. BRIZ is fully liable in cases of intent and gross negligence as well as for damages resulting from injury to life, limb or health by BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives or vicarious agents.\r\nC. BRIZ is liable under the Product Safety Act (SR 930.111).\r\nD. The liability of BRIZ, BRIZ&amp;#39;s legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents is excluded in all cases other than those mentioned in section 8.2 paragraph 1 to paragraph 3. BRIZ is released from the provision of the services, provided and insofar as the provision of force majeure is rendered impossible or considerably more difficult. BRIZ will inform the customer immediately if necessary.\r\nE. Insofar as the liability of BRIZ is limited or excluded according to the above provisions, this shall also apply to the personal liability of the legal representatives, employees and vicarious agents of BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>9. Privacy Notice</strong>\r\n\r\n9.1 BRIZ collects, processes and uses personal data which you provide during registration and use of the Services, such as your mobile phone number, email address and bank details as well as personal data related to your usage of the Vehicles, such as the place of departure, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the Services and in compliance with the provisions as set forth in the European General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”) and associated implementation provisions. This data processing is based on Art. 6 para. 1 letter b of the GDPR. Furthermore, BRIZ processes such data to identify any usage of Vehicles in breach of these ToS and/or in breach of road traffic rules and to process recourse claims for which BRIZ would be liable as the Vehicle keeper on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 letter b and c of the GDPR.\r\n\r\n9.2 BRIZ engages payment service providers for process payments. For payment by credit card, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered in England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license Nr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom. If you choose payment by credit card as your Preferred Payment Method, the credit card details you enter will be transmitted to PayAlly. PayAlly may only use these details in order to process credit card transactions that you have initiated. PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here: <a href=\"https://payally.eu/privacy-policy\">https://payally.eu/privacy-policy</a>. The data are transmitted to BRIZ´s service providers on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b of the GDPR.\r\n\r\n9.3 For further information on the use, administration, processing and storage of your personal data as well as the rights to which you are entitled in this context, please read our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n9.4 Notwithstanding provided in this clause, all the detailed information regarding your personal data is prescribed in our Privacy Policy (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>10. Changes to these ToS and Prices</strong>\r\n\r\n10.1 BRIZ expressly reserves the right to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) in accordance with the following terms.\r\n\r\n10.2 BRIZ is entitled to amend these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) at any time without giving reasons for future BRIZ Rental Contracts. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at least three days prior to such changes. BRIZ Rental Contracts included active Subscriptions that (e.g. monthly or annual pass subscription) booked prior to notification of changes will remain unaffected, subject to the ToS set forth below.\r\n\r\n10.3 In case of monthly Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract month. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract month. All notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned consequences in the change notification.\r\n\r\n10.4 In case of annual Subscriptions, BRIZ is entitled to change these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink) without giving reasons with effect to the next contract year. BRIZ will notify you of any such changes at least three days prior to the end of the current contract year. All notified changes are considered as accepted if you do not contradict this within one week after communication in text form (eg e-mail). If you disagree with the changes, the Subscription will automatically terminate. BRIZ will particularly draw your attention to the aforementioned consequences in the change notification. BRIZ is only entitled to these ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) change for the current contractual year if such change is necessary due to a change in the underlying technical, economic or legal environment. All notified changes with effect for the current contract year become effective and are considered accepted if you do not object within six weeks after notification of the changes in writing (e.g. e-mail). BRIZ will particularly draw attention to the consequences above in the notification of the changes. If mandatory changes are required by applicable law, court orders or official orders, the above deadline may be shorter in individual cases. If you object to changes with effect for the current contract year, the ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) remain unchanged in force. However, in this case, BRIZ is entitled to terminate the framework contract and the annual Subscription within three days of receipt of your opposition with a notice period of three days.\r\n\r\n10.5 BRIZ will notify you of any changes pursuant to section 10.2 to 10.4 by email, SMS or notification within the BRIZ App and by the publication of the new ToS and prices on the BRIZ Website and in the BRIZ App.\r\n\r\n10.6 Notwithstanding the above, deviating agreements to these ToS and/or the Price List (hyperlink) are only valid and binding if agreed between you and BRIZ in writing. This also applies to this text form requirement.\r\n\r\n<strong>11. Content of Third Parties</strong>\r\n\r\n11.1 While using the BRIZ App, you may come into contact with third parties, advertisers or sponsors and/or their content, goods and/or services. We are not responsible for any third party services.\r\n\r\n11.2 BRIZ has no influence on the content of external pages linked via the BRIZ App or the BRIZ Website and is not responsible for this.\r\n\r\n<strong>12. Applicable Law</strong>\r\n\r\nThe agreement, including these ToS and the Price List (hyperlink), shall be governed by the laws of Switzerland, for customers using our Services in Switzerland.\r\n\r\n<strong>13. Transfer</strong>\r\n\r\n13.1 BRIZ is entitled to assign its rights and obligations as specified in these ToS to a third party at any time without your consent. However, BRIZ is obliged to inform you in good time before such a transfer in text form. In the event of such notice, you will be entitled to terminate the BRIZ Rental Contract extraordinarily within six (6) weeks of notice.\r\n\r\n13.2 You are not entitled to transfer rights or obligations under the BRIZ Rental Contract to third parties or assign them to third parties without the prior written consent of BRIZ.\r\n\r\n<strong>14. No Waiver</strong>\r\n\r\nIf and insofar BRIZ waives all or part of the enforcement of individual provisions of these ToS, this does not constitute a waiver of the subsequent assertion and the validity of these ToS.\r\n\r\n<strong>15. Validity</strong>\r\n\r\nShould one or more provisions of these ToS or the current Price List (hyperlink) be declared invalid or void by a court, this shall not affect the remaining provisions of these ToS and/or Price List (hyperlink).\r\n\r\n<strong>16. Remark of Dispute</strong>\r\n\r\nBRIZ is not obliged nor willing to participate in dispute resolution proceedings before a Federal Consumer Affairs Bureau (FCAB). See the European Online Dispute Resolution Platform <a href=\"https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage\">https://ec.europa.eu/consumers/odr/main/index.cfm?event=main.home.chooseLanguage</a> on alternative dispute resolution.\r\n\r\n<strong>17. Customer Service</strong>\r\n\r\nIf you have questions about or have a problem with our services, you can contact us through the BRIZ App by clicking on the &amp;quot;Customer Service&amp;quot; button. You can also contact BRIZ by e-mail (hello@briz.app).\r\n\r\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.\r\nMay 2019',	'Terms&Conditions',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'26-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:38:20',	'2019-05-14 14:38:20',	'',	26,	'https://briz.app/26-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(204,	1,	'2019-05-16 14:55:57',	'2019-05-16 11:55:57',	'Last updated on 01 May 2019\n\nAt BRIZ, we are committed to protecting your privacy. Please, read this Privacy Policy to become familiar with further details of our approaches towards your personal data.\n\n<b>What we need and why?</b>\n\nOur Privacy Policy governs the processing of your personal data, including but not limited to collection, process, use, storage, transfer etc. connected with your use of services, as defined in our <a href=\"https://briz.app/termsconditions/\">Terms of Use</a>.\n\n<b>What do we do with it?</b>\n\nWe process your personal data. No third party providers have access to your personal data unless specifically required by law or duly encrypted.\n\n<b>1. Responsible Controller </b>\n\nBRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (hereinafter: “we” or “BRIZ“) is the operator both of the Website <a href=\"http://www.briz.app\">www.briz.app</a> (hereinafter, the “Website”) and the BRIZ app (hereinafter, the “Application”) and therefore the responsible party of the personal data of the users (hereinafter: “you”, “your” “users” or “users”) of the Website and the Application in terms of the General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”).\n\n<b>2. Contact </b>\n\nIf you have any questions regarding the use of your personal data, please do not hesitate to contact us at <a href=\"mailto:hello@briz.app\">hello@briz.app</a> or via our customer service hotline.\n\n<b>3. General Info and Personal Data</b>\n\n3.1 We protect your privacy and your personal data. We collect, process, and use your personal data in accordance with the content of this Privacy Policy and the GDPR and only as far as this is necessary to provide a functional Website and Application as well as our content and services.\n\n3.2 Personal data within the meaning of this Privacy Policy means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person. This includes the personal data required for registration in the Application and its usage, such as:\n<ul>\n 	<li>your name,</li>\n 	<li>telephone number,</li>\n 	<li>billing information</li>\n 	<li>location,</li>\n 	<li>camera`s access,</li>\n 	<li>information about the WLAN connection,</li>\n 	<li>information about Bluetooth connection,</li>\n 	<li>the IP-address of your computer/phone,</li>\n 	<li>the operating system of your computer/phone,</li>\n 	<li>the type of browser you are using (Firefox, Google Chrome, etc.) and its version,</li>\n 	<li>the request of your browser,</li>\n 	<li>the time of this request,</li>\n 	<li>the status of the request,</li>\n 	<li>the amount of personal data transferred in the context of this request,</li>\n 	<li>date and time of access,</li>\n 	<li>the URL of the Website from which you accessed our Website (so-called referrer URL),</li>\n 	<li>the URL of the Website you are visiting from our Website.</li>\n 	<li>your device and card identification,</li>\n 	<li>the name of your telephone, if you have named it using your own name,</li>\n 	<li>the quantity of the transferred personal data with respect to that request,</li>\n 	<li>personal data related to usage of the Electric Scooter, such as the place of departure, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the BRIZ`s services as stated in its Terms of Service.</li>\n</ul>\n&nbsp;\n\n3.3 Personal data also includes information about your use of our Website and the Application. This includes, for example, information about the location from which you access data from our Website or Application or the extent of the data transfer. This personal data is usually processed using server log files and cookies.\n\n<b>4. Processing Purposes</b>\n\n4.1 Your personal data will be processed in order to allow access to the services provided by BRIZ and to have access to information hosted on our Website and the Application and provide the information and the services requested by you in the Application and in the Website.\n\n4.2 We process your personal data to comply with the legal obligations that we are subject to.\n\n4.3 We will also process your personal data for sending commercial communications in the case that you have authorized us to do so.\n\n4.4 In addition, we can process your personal data in the following cases:\n<ul>\n 	<li>in order to reply to any request you may send to us,</li>\n 	<li>in order to understand your needs, provide services that are relevant to you and boost the quality of our services,</li>\n 	<li>in order to communicate with you as a possible member of our great team.</li>\n</ul>\n<b>5. Origin and Legal Basis for the Processing of Your Personal Data</b>\n\n5.1 The personal data that we process has been provided by you.\n\n5.2 Some personal data may only be processed with your consent in accordance with Art. 6 para. 1 lit. a GDPR. You can withdraw this consent at any time for the future. \"For the future\" means that your withdrawal has no effect on the processing of personal data that we have made between the granting of your consent and your withdrawal. You do not have to justify your withdrawal. An informal message via e-mail to <a href=\"mailto:hello@briz.app\">hello@briz.app</a>. is sufficient.\n\n5.3 We process personal data that we require to fulfil or conclude a contract with you or to carry out pre-contractual measures on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR.\n\n5.4 Other personal data we process according to Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f. GDPR for the protection of our legitimate interests, e.g. for the technically error-free and optimized provision of our services.\n\n5.5 It may be also necessary to process personal data in order to fulfil a legal obligation that we are subject to (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. c GDPR) or to protect your vital interests (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. d GDPR).\n\n5.6 In addition, we may be legally process your personal data when the following applies:\n<ul>\n 	<li>processing is necessary to provide you our services according to our Terms of Service, which constitutes a contract between you and us as regards to information services of our Website;</li>\n 	<li>processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by us or by a third party on the conditions prescribed by the data protection legislation;</li>\n 	<li>processing is necessary for compliance with our legal obligations;</li>\n 	<li>processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in us.</li>\n</ul>\n<b>6. Recipients</b>\n\nYour personal data may be transferred to public administrations, including courts, when it is required in accordance with the current legislation in force. Additionally, companies that provide services to us and are contracted by BRIZ, such as payment providers, can have access to your personal data. To the extent BRIZ uses such contractors, a description of their services can be found below. Unless noted otherwise below, these external companies process data for BRIZ as data processors, i.e. based on BRIZ’s instructions.\n\n<b>7. Duration of Storage</b>\n\nYour personal data will be kept as long as it is necessary for the purposes established in this policy. However, it may happen that the European or national legislator requires a longer storage period. In these cases, the personal data is not deleted or locked until the corresponding retention period has expired. After this period, the personal data will be definitively deleted.\n\n<b>8. Download / Installation of the Application</b>\n\n8.1 When you download/install our Application, we will ask for permission to use interfaces to access functions and contents of your device in order to collect certain personal data including:\n\n- your location,\n\n- your camera`s access,\n\n- information about the WLAN connection,\n\n- information about your Bluetooth connection (possibly).\n\n8.2 Since we require the personal data to fulfil our contract with you, the legal basis is Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR.\n\n8.3 We need access to the above interfaces and personal data in order to provide you with the functions and services of our Application and thus to fulfil our obligations under the general agreement as well as to enable the booking of an Electric Scooter. For example, your location is needed to show you the next Electric Scooter in your area and how to get there. In addition, if you rent an Electric Scooter, we track your location when locking and unlocking the Scooter. If a Scooter is rented, we retrieve the location of the Scooter directly via a GPS module integrated into the Scooters and not via your device. Location tracking only takes place to ensure a proper lending and return process or to assist you in the event you report a service case.\n\n8.4 Access is possible from the moment the Application is installed on your mobile device. Depending on your settings, this access is permanent or only for the duration of the actual use of the Application. For the highest possible level of personal data protection, we recommend that you only allow access during the actual use of the Application. The personal data retrieved in each case are generally stored only for the duration of the actual use of the Application. We store your location retrieved in the event you report a service case for a maximum duration of one year at the time of reporting. We store the location data that we collect in connection with locking and unlocking our Electric Scooters for a maximum duration of 3 years. The location data will then be made anonymous or will be blocked and deleted according to the rules stated in clause 7 of this Policy regarding “Duration of the Storage”.\n\n<b>9. Google Maps, Google Analytics and Amazon Web Services</b>\n\n9.1 Our Application uses Google Maps API applications. This is a service of Google LLC, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA. In this context, we must store your IP address. Usually, this information is transferred to a Google server in the USA and stored there. However, this transmission is made anonymous and Google LLC has subscribed to the EU-U.S. Privacy Shield Framework. A conclusion on your person is thus excluded. This enables us to display interactive maps directly in the Application and enables you to use the map functions. This application is essential for the functionality and complete provision of our content and services. You can view the Google Terms of Use here: <a href=\"https://policies.google.com/terms?hl=en\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://policies.google.com/terms?hl=en</u></span></a>. The additional terms of use for Google Maps/Google Earth can be found here: <a href=\"https://www.google.com/help/terms_maps.html\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://www.google.com/help/terms_maps.html</u></span></a>. You can find Google\'s privacy policy here: <a href=\"https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en-GB\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en-GB</u></span></a>.\n\n9.2 We use Google Analytics. This is an analysis tool provided by <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">Google Inc, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA. Google Inc</span>, has subscribed to the EU-U.S. Privacy Shield Framework. We use this technology to make our Website more interesting for you and to optimize its functionality. The following personal data is processed in this context:\n\n- the IP address of your computer,\n\n- if necessary, the operating system of your computer,\n\n- the type of browser you are using (Firefox, Google Chrome, etc.) and its version,\n\n- the referrer URL,\n\n- the time of the request.\n\n9.3 We use Amazon <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">Web Services Inc. 410 Terry Avenue North, Seattle WA 98109, USA</span>. Amazon Web Services Inc. has subscribed to the EU-U.S. Privacy Shield Framework. In this context, information is transmitted exclusively to servers in and stored with Amazon Web Service.\n\nAmazon may not use the personal data for other purposes. In addition, Amazon is obliged to treat the information in accordance with this data protection declaration and the relevant data protection laws.\n\nMore information can be found in Amazon\'s privacy policy: <a href=\"https://services.amazon.com/privacy-policy.html\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://services.amazon.com/privacy-policy.html</u></span></a>.\n\n9.4 These personal data are processed on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR for the conclusion and performance of a contract as well as a legitimate interest in improving the services of our Website and our advertising.\n\n9.5 We process this personal data to show you the location of the nearest Electric Scooter and how to get there. Furthermore, we can show you the expected running distance and running time to the selected Electric Scooter.\n\n9.6 In addition the purpose of the processing is our legitimate interest in improving the services of our Website and our advertising.\n\n9.7 The personal data will only be stored for the duration of the respective booking period and will then be deleted.\n\n9.8 If you only wish to accept our own cookies, but not those of our service providers and partners, you can select the setting in your browser \"Block third-party cookies\".\n\n<b>10. Registration with your Telephone Number, Facebook Connect or Google Authentication</b>\n\n10.1 In order to use our Application, you have to register. You can register by entering your telephone number in the input screen provided for this purpose.\n\n10.2 You also have the option to register in our Application via Facebook Connect. This is a service of <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">Facebook Ireland Limited, 4 Grand Canal Square, Dublin 2, Ireland.</span> As the registration is performed through Facebook Connect BRIZ cannot control the procedure to sign on in the registration. For that reason, BRIZ dissociates from any responsibility arising from any breach, action or inaction of Facebook Connect or any breach of third parties that can be performed in the registration procedure. By clicking on the button integrated into our Application for this purpose, you can register with your Facebook login data and thus speed up the login process. This process links our Application to your Facebook profile and you consent to the processing of the public data on your Facebook profile.\n\n10.3. You also have the option to register in our Application via Google Authentication. This is a service of <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">Google Inc, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA. Google Inc</span>. As the registration is performed through Google Authentication BRIZ cannot control the procedure to sign on in the registration. For that reason, BRIZ dissociates from any responsibility arising from any breach, action or inaction of Google Authentication or any breach of third parties that can be performed in the registration procedure. By clicking on the button integrated into our Application for this purpose, you can register with your Google login data and thus speed up the login process. This process links our Application to your Google profile and you consent to the processing of the public data on your Google profile.\n\n10.4 The personal data will be processed with your consent and therefore on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. a GDPR. You can revoke your consent at any time for the future. \"For the future\" means that your revocation has no effect on the processing of personal data that we have made between the granting of your consent and your revocation. You do not have to give reasons for your revocation. An informal message by e-mail to us is sufficient.\n\n10.5 The processing of your personal data during registration is carried out on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR for the conclusion and fulfilment of a contract.\n\n10.6 These personal data are processed solely in order to provide you with the functionality of our Application. Without registration as a user, there is no way to rent and use an Electric Scooter through the Application.\n\n10.7 As soon as you uninstall the Application and the legal retention periods have expired, the personal data entered during registration will be deleted.\n\n<b>11. Payment Method Credit Card via PayAlly, Stripe, PayPal, Apple Pay and Google Pay.</b>\n\n11.1 As soon as you have registered by one way or the other, you have the possibility to choose a payment method. For payment by credit card, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered in England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license Nr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom.\n\nIf you decide to pay via PayAlly, the personal data you enter will be transmitted to PayAlly for payment during sign-up. PayAlly may not use them for other purposes. PayAlly is also subject to bank client confidentiality and is obliged to treat the information in accordance with the relevant data protection laws.\n\nPayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here: <a href=\"https://payally.eu/privacy-policy\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://payally.eu/privacy-policy</u></span></a>.\n\n11.2 In addition, we can use the payment service provider Stripe, Stripe, Inc. 185 Berry Street, Suite 550 San Francisco, CA 94107, USA; or PayPal, PayPal (Europe) S.à r.l et Cie, S.C.A., so you can also pay via your PayPal account.\n\nIf you choose to pay via Stripe or PayPal, the information you provide will be sent to Stripe or PayPal for payment at sign-up. Stripe or PayPal may not use them for other purposes. In addition, Stripe or PayPal is required to treat the information in accordance with this Privacy Policy and the applicable data protection laws.\n\nYou can find Stripe’s privacy policy here: <a href=\"https://stripe.com/de/privacy\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://stripe.com/de/privacy</u></span></a>.\n\nYou can find PayPal\'s privacy policy here: <a href=\"https://www.paypal.com/ch/webapps/mpp/ua/privacy-full?locale.x=de_CH\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://www.paypal.com/ch/webapps/mpp/ua/privacy-full?locale.x=de_CH</u></span></a>.\n\nPayPal may pre-authorize your PayPal account on behalf of BRIZ by debiting your users account with EUR 1, but this amount will be refunded immediately.\n\n11.3 In addition, we use the payment service provider Apple Pay of Apple lnc., so iOS users can pay via your Apple Pay account.\n\nYou can find Apple Pay\'s security and privacy overview here: <a href=\"https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT203027\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT203027</u></span></a>\n\nYou can find Apple’s Privacy Policy here:\n\n<a href=\"https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/</u></span></a>\n\n11.4 In addition, we use the payment service provider Google Pay of Google lnc., so Android users can pay via your Google Pay account.\n\nYou can find Google’s Privacy Policy here: <a href=\"https://policies.google.com/privacy\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://policies.google.com/privacy</u></span></a>.\n\n11.5 The personal data are transmitted on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR for the conclusion and performance of a contract.\n\n11.6 The personal data are transmitted exclusively for the purpose of providing you with the functions and services of our Application. Without depositing a method to pay the rental price of an Electric Scooter (both for single trips and for subscriptions or to top up your credit in the Application), there is no way to rent and use an Electric Scooter through the Application.\n\n11.7 All the payment data is stored by PayAlly and PayAlly or other payment operator mentioned above itself. Please also note PayAlly’s and other privacy policy linked above.\n\n11.8 The users have the right to receive, free of charges, the corresponding invoices if it is requested.\n\n<b>12. Using BRIZ Website and Application</b>\n\n12.1 Whenever you access our Website, we collect the following information about your computer:\n\n- the IP-address of your computer,\n\n- the operating system of your computer,\n\n- the type of browser you are using (Firefox, Google Chrome, etc.) and its version,\n\n- the request of your browser,\n\n- the time of this request,\n\n- the status of the request,\n\n- the amount of personal data transferred in the context of this request,\n\n- Date and time of access,\n\n- the URL of the Website from which you accessed our Website (so-called referrer URL),\n\n- the URL of the Website you are visiting from our Website.\n\n12.2 Every time you open our Application, we collect so-called server log files. These personal data log all requests and accessed by visitors to the Application and record all error messages from an Application. These include:\n\n- the IP address of your mobile device,\n\n- your device and card identification,\n\n- the name of your telephone, if you have named it using your own name,\n\n- the time of the request,\n\n- the status of the request,\n\n- the quantity of the transferred personal data with respect to that request.\n\n12.3 The legal basis for this is Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR. The operator of Application has a legitimate interest in the storage of this personal data because he needs it to detect and eliminate errors of the Website and Application, to determine the utilization of the Website and the Application or to make improvements.\n\n12.4 The purpose of this type of personal data processing results from our legitimate interest mentioned above: This personal data is processed to detect and eliminate Website and Application errors in order to determine the utilization of the Website and Application or to make improvements.\n\n12.5 The IP address of your computer will only be stored for the duration of your visit and will subsequently be deleted immediately or made anonymous by shortening it. The remaining personal data is stored anonymously for an unlimited period of time.\n\n12.6 The personal data will be deleted as soon as you close our Application.\n\n12.7 The privacy of children is one of our concerns. Here at BRIZ we can provide services only in case you are aged 16 or older. If you are under 16 you will need to get your parent’s/guardian’s permission before submission of any personal data to BRIZ. If you are underage, and there are no data as to your parent’s/guardian’s permission to use our Website and Application, we will not collect or process your personal data, and you will have limited/restricted use of our Website and Application.\n\n<b>13. Cookies</b>\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in;\" align=\"RIGHT\"><i>We explain here what cookies are, how we use cookies, your choices regarding cookies and further information about cookies.</i></p>\n&nbsp;\n\n13.1 Does BRIZ use cookies?\n\nYes. BRIZ uses cookies and other technologies on our Website and within our related services. By using our Website or our related services, you consent to the use of cookies for the purposes we describe in this policy.\n\n13.2 What are cookies and how do they work?\n\nCookies are small files comprising bits of text that are installed on your computer or mobile device each time you open a Website. These small files enable users to authenticate themselves on successive visits to the Website and gain access to the services.\n\nYour browser tells our systems if any cookies files were installed in your computer and after our software systems connect to the cookies we are able to analyze the information the cookies files give us.\n\n13.3 What cookies does BRIZ use and for what purposes?\n\nWe use the personal data we process using technically unnecessary cookies to tailor our Website to your individual interests. This includes, for example, advertising that corresponds to your personal interests.\n\n13.4 What is the duration of cookies storage with BRIZ?\n\nThe duration of storage varies depending on whether the cookies are session cookies or temporary cookies. Session cookies are automatically deleted after you leave our Website. Temporary cookies are stored on your device for a certain period. Cookies that we use for statistical purposes are automatically deleted after a defined period.\n\n13.5 Can I opt-out from the use of cookies after I agreed BRIZ will use it?\n\nNo, you may not opt-out from the session cookies used within the use.\n\n13.6 What are your choices regarding cookies\n\nAs a user, you have full control over the use of cookies and the personal data processed in this way. If you do not want to use cookies, you can set your browser so that the storage of cookies will not be accepted. Please note that in this case, you may be able to use our Website only partially or not at all.\n\n13.7 Finally, please be informed that you have the right to withdraw your consent so that we cannot use cookies, setting your browser in the terms mentioned below:\n\n- If you use Microsoft Internet Explorer, in the menu option Tools, selecting Internet Options and accessing Privacy; For the Internet Explorer web browser, please visit this page from Microsoft: <a href=\"http://support.microsoft.com/kb/278835\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>http://support.microsoft.com/kb/278835</u></span></a>.\n\n- If you use Firefox for Mac in the Preferences menu option, selecting Privacy, accessing the Show Cookies section, and in the Tools menu option, selecting Options, accessing Privacy and then using a custom configuration for the history; For the Firefox web browser, please visit this page from Mozilla: <a href=\"https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/delete-cookies-remove-info-websites-stored\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/delete-cookies-remove-info-websites-stored</u></span></a>.\n\n- If you use Safari, in the Preferences menu option, selecting Privacy;\n\nFor the Safari web browser, please visit this page from Apple: <a href=\"https://support.apple.com/kb/PH21411?locale=en_US\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://support.apple.com/kb/PH21411?locale=en_US</u></span></a>.\n\n- If you use Google Chrome, in the Tools menu option, selecting Options (Preferences in Mac), accessing Advanced and then in the Content Configuration option in the Privacy section, and finally checking Cookies in the Content Settings dialogue; For the Chrome web browser, please visit this page from Google: <a href=\"https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/32050\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/32050</u></span></a>.\n\nFor any other web browser, please visit your web browser\'s official web pages.\n\n13.8 Where can you find more information about cookies?\n\nYou can learn more about cookies and the following third-party websites:\n\nAllAboutCookies: <a href=\"http://www.allaboutcookies.org/\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>http://www.allaboutcookies.org/</u></span></a>.\n\nNetwork Advertising Initiative: <a href=\"http://www.networkadvertising.org/\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>http://www.networkadvertising.org/</u></span></a>.\n\n<b>14. Personal Data Security</b>\n\n14.1 We protect our Website and Application and other systems by technical and organizational measures against loss, destruction, access, modification, or dissemination of your personal data by unauthorized persons. These measures include but are not limited to access control, input control and order control.\n\n14.2 BRIZ processes your personal data using computers and/or other IT enabled tools. BRIZ takes technical and organizational measures to ensure the information is processed in a manner that ensures appropriate security of information, including protection against unauthorized or unlawful processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. We also guide and train our personnel to process your personal data securely according to our internal personal data protection policies.\n\n<b>15. No Disclosure of Your Personal Data</b>\n\nWe will not disclose your personal data to third parties, except if you have consented to the personal data transfer or if we are authorized or obliged to transfer personal data due to legal provisions and/or official or court directions. This may refer to cases including but not limited to the provision of information for the purposes of law enforcement, danger prevention or the enforcement of intellectual property rights.\n\n<b>16. Personal Data Protection and Third-Party Websites</b>\n\n16.1 This Website may contain hyperlinks to or from third-party websites. If you follow a hyperlink to one of these websites, please note that we cannot assume any responsibility or guarantee for external contents or personal data protection conditions. Please verify the respective applicable data protection provisions before you transfer personal data to these websites.\n\n16.2 Personal data communication via the internet cannot be guaranteed to be error-free and/or available at all times according to the current state of technology. In this respect, we are not liable for the constant and uninterrupted availability of our trading system.\n\n<b>17. Amendments</b>\n\nWe reserve the right to amend this Privacy Policy at any time with future effect. The respective latest version is available at all time on the Website and the Application. Please access the Website and Application regularly to find out about the applicable Privacy Policy.\n\n<b>18. Your Rights and Contact Information</b>\n\n18.1 Right to withdraw your consent acc. Art. 7 para. 3 GDPR: In cases where the processing of your personal data is only possible with your consent, you can revoke this consent at any time in the future. \"For the Future\" means that your revocation has no effect on the processing of personal data that we have made between the granting of your consent and your revocation. You do not have to justify your withdrawal. An informal message via e-mail to us is sufficient.\n\n18.2 Right of access by the data subject in acc. Art. 15 GDPR: you may request confirmation from us at any time whether we process personal information concerning you. In this case, you have the right to request information about:\n\n- the purposes for which we process your personal information\n\n- the categories of personal data we process,\n\n- the recipients or categories of recipients to whom we have disclosed or will disclose the personal data,\n\n- the storage duration (as far as possible),\n\n- the right of rectification, erasure or restriction of our processing, as well as the right of opposition to such processing,\n\n- the existence of a right of appeal to a supervisory authority,\n\n- the origin of your personal data, as far as they were not collected by us,\n\n- the existence of automated decision-making including profiling and, where appropriate, detailed information on the logic, scope and impact of such processing.\n\nFor this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.\n\n18.3 Right to rectification acc. Art. 16 GDPR: you can view your personal data at any time free of charge and, if necessary, request their correction and supplementation.\n\nFor this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app.. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.\n\n18.4 Right to erasure acc. Art. 17 GDPR: you can view your personal data at any time free of charge and request cancellation if:\n\n- these are no longer needed for the purpose for which they were processed,\n\n- you have revoked your consent and there is no other legal basis for the processing,\n\n- you have filed an objection against the processing of your personal data acc. Art. 21 GDPR,\n\n- we have processed your personal data unlawfully,\n\n- the deletion is required to fulfil a legal obligation under EU or national law.\n\nFor this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.\n\n18.5 Right to the restriction of processing acc. Art. 18 GDPR: you can view your personal data at any time free of charge and, if necessary, request their blocking if:\n\n- you deny their accuracy,\n\n- the processing is illegal, but you reject the deletion of the personal data,\n\n- we no longer need the personal data, but you need it for the assertion, exercise or defence of legal claims,\n\n- you have filed an objection against the processing of your personal data acc. Art. 21 GDPR, but it is not yet certain whether our interests in processing outweigh your interests.\n\nFor this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.\n\n18.6 Right to data portability acc. Art. 20 GDPR: At our request, we are required to provide you with data that we process automatically based on your consent or in fulfilment of a contract in a portable and secure format. The direct transfer of personal data to another person responsible is also possible at your request. However, it only takes place if technically feasible.\n\nFor this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.\n\n18.7 Right to object acc. Art. 21 GDPR: In cases where we use your personal data on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR, you have the right to appeal against the processing, as far as there are reasons for this, which result from your particular situation or the objection against direct mailing.\n\nFor this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.\n\n18.8 Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority acc. Art. 77 GDPR: If you think that we have violated data protection regulations, you can contact a regulatory authority for personal data protection in the non-public area, in particular, the supervisory authority of your habitual residence, your work-place or the location of such violation.\n\n<b>BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.</b>\n\n<b>May 2019</b>',	'Privacy Policy',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'3-autosave-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-16 14:55:57',	'2019-05-16 11:55:57',	'',	3,	'https://briz.app/3-autosave-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
(205,	1,	'2019-05-14 17:55:30',	'2019-05-14 14:55:30',	'<p>Last updated on 01 May 2019</p>\r\n<p>At BRIZ, we are committed to protecting your privacy. Please, read this Privacy Policy to become familiar with further details of our approaches towards your personal data.</p>\r\n<p><b>What we need and why?</b></p>\r\n<p>Our Privacy Policy governs the processing of your personal data, including but not limited to collection, process, use, storage, transfer etc. connected with your use of services, as defined in our Terms of Use (<span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">hyperlink</span>).</p>\r\n<p><b>What do we do with it?</b></p>\r\n<p>We process your personal data. No third party providers have access to your personal data unless specifically required by law or duly encrypted.</p>\r\n<p><b>1. Responsible Controller </b></p>\r\n<p>BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd., Clifton House, Fitzwilliam Street Lower, Dublin 2, D02XT91, Ireland (hereinafter: “we” or “BRIZ“) is the operator both of the Website <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\"><a href=\"http://www.briz.app\">www.briz.app</a> </span>(hereinafter, the “Website”) and the BRIZ app (hereinafter, the “Application”) and therefore the responsible party of the personal data of the users (hereinafter: “you”, “your” “users” or “users”) of the Website and the Application in terms of the General Data Protection Regulation (“GDPR”).</p>\r\n<p><b>2. Contact </b></p>\r\n<p>If you have any questions regarding the use of your personal data, please do not hesitate to contact us at <a href=\"mailto:hello@briz.app\">hello@briz.app</a> or via our customer service hotline.</p>\r\n<p><b>3. General Info and Personal Data</b></p>\r\n<p>3.1 We protect your privacy and your personal data. We collect, process, and use your personal data in accordance with the content of this Privacy Policy and the GDPR and only as far as this is necessary to provide a functional Website and Application as well as our content and services.</p>\r\n<p>3.2 Personal data within the meaning of this Privacy Policy means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person. This includes the personal data required for registration in the Application and its usage, such as:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>your name,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>telephone number,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>billing information</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>location,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>camera`s access,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>information about the WLAN connection,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>information about Bluetooth connection,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the IP-address of your computer/phone,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the operating system of your computer/phone,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the type of browser you are using (Firefox, Google Chrome, etc.) and its version,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the request of your browser,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the time of this request,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the status of the request,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the amount of personal data transferred in the context of this request,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>date and time of access,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the URL of the Website from which you accessed our Website (so-called referrer URL),</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the URL of the Website you are visiting from our Website.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>your device and card identification,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the name of your telephone, if you have named it using your own name,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>the quantity of the transferred personal data with respect to that request,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>personal data related to usage of the Electric Scooter, such as the place of departure, arrival, rental period, insofar as required for performance of the BRIZ`s services as stated in its Terms of Service.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>3.3 Personal data also includes information about your use of our Website and the Application. This includes, for example, information about the location from which you access data from our Website or Application or the extent of the data transfer. This personal data is usually processed using server log files and cookies.</p>\r\n<p><b>4. Processing Purposes</b></p>\r\n<p>4.1 Your personal data will be processed in order to allow access to the services provided by BRIZ and to have access to information hosted on our Website and the Application and provide the information and the services requested by you in the Application and in the Website.</p>\r\n<p>4.2 We process your personal data to comply with the legal obligations that we are subject to.</p>\r\n<p>4.3 We will also process your personal data for sending commercial communications in the case that you have authorized us to do so.</p>\r\n<p>4.4 In addition, we can process your personal data in the following cases:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>in order to reply to any request you may send to us,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>in order to understand your needs, provide services that are relevant to you and boost the quality of our services,</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>in order to communicate with you as a possible member of our great team.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><b>5. Origin and Legal Basis for the Processing of Your Personal Data</b></p>\r\n<p>5.1 The personal data that we process has been provided by you.</p>\r\n<p>5.2 Some personal data may only be processed with your consent in accordance with Art. 6 para. 1 lit. a GDPR. You can withdraw this consent at any time for the future. \"For the future\" means that your withdrawal has no effect on the processing of personal data that we have made between the granting of your consent and your withdrawal. You do not have to justify your withdrawal. An informal message via e-mail to <a href=\"mailto:hello@briz.app\">hello@briz.app</a>. is sufficient.</p>\r\n<p>5.3 We process personal data that we require to fulfil or conclude a contract with you or to carry out pre-contractual measures on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR.</p>\r\n<p>5.4 Other personal data we process according to Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f. GDPR for the protection of our legitimate interests, e.g. for the technically error-free and optimized provision of our services.</p>\r\n<p>5.5 It may be also necessary to process personal data in order to fulfil a legal obligation that we are subject to (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. c GDPR) or to protect your vital interests (Art. 6 para. 1 lit. d GDPR).</p>\r\n<p>5.6 In addition, we may be legally process your personal data when the following applies:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>processing is necessary to provide you our services according to our Terms of Service, which constitutes a contract between you and us as regards to information services of our Website;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>processing is necessary for the purposes of the legitimate interests pursued by us or by a third party on the conditions prescribed by the data protection legislation;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>processing is necessary for compliance with our legal obligations;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p>processing is necessary for the performance of a task carried out in the public interest or in the exercise of official authority vested in us.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><b>6. Recipients</b></p>\r\n<p>Your personal data may be transferred to public administrations, including courts, when it is required in accordance with the current legislation in force. Additionally, companies that provide services to us and are contracted by BRIZ, such as payment providers, can have access to your personal data. To the extent BRIZ uses such contractors, a description of their services can be found below. Unless noted otherwise below, these external companies process data for BRIZ as data processors, i.e. based on BRIZ’s instructions.</p>\r\n<p><b>7. Duration of Storage</b></p>\r\n<p>Your personal data will be kept as long as it is necessary for the purposes established in this policy. However, it may happen that the European or national legislator requires a longer storage period. In these cases, the personal data is not deleted or locked until the corresponding retention period has expired. After this period, the personal data will be definitively deleted.</p>\r\n<p><b>8. Download / Installation of the Application</b></p>\r\n<p>8.1 When you download/install our Application, we will ask for permission to use interfaces to access functions and contents of your device in order to collect certain personal data including:</p>\r\n<p>- your location,</p>\r\n<p>- your camera`s access,</p>\r\n<p>- information about the WLAN connection,</p>\r\n<p>- information about your Bluetooth connection (possibly).</p>\r\n<p>8.2 Since we require the personal data to fulfil our contract with you, the legal basis is Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR.</p>\r\n<p>8.3 We need access to the above interfaces and personal data in order to provide you with the functions and services of our Application and thus to fulfil our obligations under the general agreement as well as to enable the booking of an Electric Scooter. For example, your location is needed to show you the next Electric Scooter in your area and how to get there. In addition, if you rent an Electric Scooter, we track your location when locking and unlocking the Scooter. If a Scooter is rented, we retrieve the location of the Scooter directly via a GPS module integrated into the Scooters and not via your device. Location tracking only takes place to ensure a proper lending and return process or to assist you in the event you report a service case.</p>\r\n<p>8.4 Access is possible from the moment the Application is installed on your mobile device. Depending on your settings, this access is permanent or only for the duration of the actual use of the Application. For the highest possible level of personal data protection, we recommend that you only allow access during the actual use of the Application. The personal data retrieved in each case are generally stored only for the duration of the actual use of the Application. We store your location retrieved in the event you report a service case for a maximum duration of one year at the time of reporting. We store the location data that we collect in connection with locking and unlocking our Electric Scooters for a maximum duration of 3 years. The location data will then be made anonymous or will be blocked and deleted according to the rules stated in clause 7 of this Policy regarding “Duration of the Storage”.</p>\r\n<p><b>9. Google Maps, Google Analytics and Amazon Web Services</b></p>\r\n<p>9.1 Our Application uses Google Maps API applications. <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">This is a service of Google LLC, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA.</span> In this context, we must store your IP address. Usually, this information is transferred to a Google server in the USA and stored there. However, this transmission is made anonymous and Google LLC has subscribed to the EU-U.S. Privacy Shield Framework. A conclusion on your person is thus excluded. This enables us to display interactive maps directly in the Application and enables you to use the map functions. This application is essential for the functionality and complete provision of our content and services. You can view the Google Terms of Use here: <a href=\"https://policies.google.com/terms?hl=en\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://policies.google.com/terms?hl=en</u></span></a>. The additional terms of use for Google Maps/Google Earth can be found here: <a href=\"https://www.google.com/help/terms_maps.html\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://www.google.com/help/terms_maps.html</u></span></a>. You can find Google\'s privacy policy here: <a href=\"https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en-GB\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en-GB</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>9.2 We use Google Analytics. This is an analysis tool provided by <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">Google Inc, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA. Google Inc</span>, has subscribed to the EU-U.S. Privacy Shield Framework. We use this technology to make our Website more interesting for you and to optimize its functionality. The following personal data is processed in this context:</p>\r\n<p>- the IP address of your computer,</p>\r\n<p>- if necessary, the operating system of your computer,</p>\r\n<p>- the type of browser you are using (Firefox, Google Chrome, etc.) and its version,</p>\r\n<p>- the referrer URL,</p>\r\n<p>- the time of the request.</p>\r\n<p>9.3 We use Amazon <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">Web Services Inc. 410 Terry Avenue North, Seattle WA 98109, USA</span>. Amazon Web Services Inc. has subscribed to the EU-U.S. Privacy Shield Framework. In this context, information is transmitted exclusively to servers in and stored with Amazon Web Service.</p>\r\n<p>Amazon may not use the personal data for other purposes. In addition, Amazon is obliged to treat the information in accordance with this data protection declaration and the relevant data protection laws.</p>\r\n<p>More information can be found in Amazon\'s privacy policy: <a href=\"https://services.amazon.com/privacy-policy.html\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://services.amazon.com/privacy-policy.html</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>9.4 These personal data are processed on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR for the conclusion and performance of a contract as well as a legitimate interest in improving the services of our Website and our advertising.</p>\r\n<p>9.5 We process this personal data to show you the location of the nearest Electric Scooter and how to get there. Furthermore, we can show you the expected running distance and running time to the selected Electric Scooter.</p>\r\n<p>9.6 In addition the purpose of the processing is our legitimate interest in improving the services of our Website and our advertising.</p>\r\n<p>9.7 The personal data will only be stored for the duration of the respective booking period and will then be deleted.</p>\r\n<p>9.8 If you only wish to accept our own cookies, but not those of our service providers and partners, you can select the setting in your browser \"Block third-party cookies\".</p>\r\n<p><b>10. Registration with your Telephone Number, Facebook Connect or Google Authentication</b></p>\r\n<p>10.1 In order to use our Application, you have to register. You can register by entering your telephone number in the input screen provided for this purpose.</p>\r\n<p>10.2 You also have the option to register in our Application via Facebook Connect. This is a service of <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">Facebook Ireland Limited, 4 Grand Canal Square, Dublin 2, Ireland.</span> As the registration is performed through Facebook Connect BRIZ cannot control the procedure to sign on in the registration. For that reason, BRIZ dissociates from any responsibility arising from any breach, action or inaction of Facebook Connect or any breach of third parties that can be performed in the registration procedure. By clicking on the button integrated into our Application for this purpose, you can register with your Facebook login data and thus speed up the login process. This process links our Application to your Facebook profile and you consent to the processing of the public data on your Facebook profile.</p>\r\n<p>10.3. You also have the option to register in our Application via Google Authentication. This is a service of <span style=\"background: #ffff00;\">Google Inc, 1600 Amphitheatre Parkway, Mountain View, CA 94043, USA. Google Inc</span>. As the registration is performed through Google Authentication BRIZ cannot control the procedure to sign on in the registration. For that reason, BRIZ dissociates from any responsibility arising from any breach, action or inaction of Google Authentication or any breach of third parties that can be performed in the registration procedure. By clicking on the button integrated into our Application for this purpose, you can register with your Google login data and thus speed up the login process. This process links our Application to your Google profile and you consent to the processing of the public data on your Google profile.</p>\r\n<p>10.4 The personal data will be processed with your consent and therefore on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. a GDPR. You can revoke your consent at any time for the future. \"For the future\" means that your revocation has no effect on the processing of personal data that we have made between the granting of your consent and your revocation. You do not have to give reasons for your revocation. An informal message by e-mail to us is sufficient.</p>\r\n<p>10.5 The processing of your personal data during registration is carried out on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR for the conclusion and fulfilment of a contract.</p>\r\n<p>10.6 These personal data are processed solely in order to provide you with the functionality of our Application. Without registration as a user, there is no way to rent and use an Electric Scooter through the Application.</p>\r\n<p>10.7 As soon as you uninstall the Application and the legal retention periods have expired, the personal data entered during registration will be deleted.</p>\r\n<p><b>11. Payment Method Credit Card via PayAlly, Stripe, PayPal, Apple Pay and Google Pay.</b></p>\r\n<p>11.1 As soon as you have registered by one way or the other, you have the possibility to choose a payment method. For payment by credit card, we use the payment service provider PayAlly, PayAlly Limited is a company registered in England and Wales (company number 10600055), Authorized Payment Institution license Nr. 774327 issued by Financial Conduct Authority of United Kingdom.</p>\r\n<p>If you decide to pay via PayAlly, the personal data you enter will be transmitted to PayAlly for payment during sign-up. PayAlly may not use them for other purposes. PayAlly is also subject to bank client confidentiality and is obliged to treat the information in accordance with the relevant data protection laws.</p>\r\n<p>PayAlly’s privacy policy can be found here: <a href=\"https://payally.eu/privacy-policy\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://payally.eu/privacy-policy</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>11.2 In addition, we can use the payment service provider Stripe, Stripe, Inc. 185 Berry Street, Suite 550 San Francisco, CA 94107, USA; or PayPal, PayPal (Europe) S.à r.l et Cie, S.C.A., so you can also pay via your PayPal account.</p>\r\n<p>If you choose to pay via Stripe or PayPal, the information you provide will be sent to Stripe or PayPal for payment at sign-up. Stripe or PayPal may not use them for other purposes. In addition, Stripe or PayPal is required to treat the information in accordance with this Privacy Policy and the applicable data protection laws.</p>\r\n<p>You can find Stripe’s privacy policy here: <a href=\"https://stripe.com/de/privacy\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://stripe.com/de/privacy</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>You can find PayPal\'s privacy policy here: <a href=\"https://www.paypal.com/ch/webapps/mpp/ua/privacy-full?locale.x=de_CH\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://www.paypal.com/ch/webapps/mpp/ua/privacy-full?locale.x=de_CH</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>PayPal may pre-authorize your PayPal account on behalf of BRIZ by debiting your users account with EUR 1, but this amount will be refunded immediately.</p>\r\n<p>11.3 In addition, we use the payment service provider Apple Pay of Apple lnc., so iOS users can pay via your Apple Pay account.</p>\r\n<p>You can find Apple Pay\'s security and privacy overview here: <a href=\"https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT203027\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT203027</u></span></a></p>\r\n<p>You can find Apple’s Privacy Policy here:</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/en-ww/</u></span></a></p>\r\n<p>11.4 In addition, we use the payment service provider Google Pay of Google lnc., so Android users can pay via your Google Pay account.</p>\r\n<p>You can find Google’s Privacy Policy here: <a href=\"https://policies.google.com/privacy\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://policies.google.com/privacy</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>11.5 The personal data are transmitted on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. b GDPR for the conclusion and performance of a contract.</p>\r\n<p>11.6 The personal data are transmitted exclusively for the purpose of providing you with the functions and services of our Application. Without depositing a method to pay the rental price of an Electric Scooter (both for single trips and for subscriptions or to top up your credit in the Application), there is no way to rent and use an Electric Scooter through the Application.</p>\r\n<p>11.7 All the payment data is stored by PayAlly and PayAlly or other payment operator mentioned above itself. Please also note PayAlly’s and other privacy policy linked above.</p>\r\n<p>11.8 The users have the right to receive, free of charges, the corresponding invoices if it is requested.</p>\r\n<p><b>12. Using BRIZ Website and Application</b></p>\r\n<p>12.1 Whenever you access our Website, we collect the following information about your computer:</p>\r\n<p>- the IP-address of your computer,</p>\r\n<p>- the operating system of your computer,</p>\r\n<p>- the type of browser you are using (Firefox, Google Chrome, etc.) and its version,</p>\r\n<p>- the request of your browser,</p>\r\n<p>- the time of this request,</p>\r\n<p>- the status of the request,</p>\r\n<p>- the amount of personal data transferred in the context of this request,</p>\r\n<p>- Date and time of access,</p>\r\n<p>- the URL of the Website from which you accessed our Website (so-called referrer URL),</p>\r\n<p>- the URL of the Website you are visiting from our Website.</p>\r\n<p>12.2 Every time you open our Application, we collect so-called server log files. These personal data log all requests and accessed by visitors to the Application and record all error messages from an Application. These include:</p>\r\n<p>- the IP address of your mobile device,</p>\r\n<p>- your device and card identification,</p>\r\n<p>- the name of your telephone, if you have named it using your own name,</p>\r\n<p>- the time of the request,</p>\r\n<p>- the status of the request,</p>\r\n<p>- the quantity of the transferred personal data with respect to that request.</p>\r\n<p>12.3 The legal basis for this is Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR. The operator of Application has a legitimate interest in the storage of this personal data because he needs it to detect and eliminate errors of the Website and Application, to determine the utilization of the Website and the Application or to make improvements.</p>\r\n<p>12.4 The purpose of this type of personal data processing results from our legitimate interest mentioned above: This personal data is processed to detect and eliminate Website and Application errors in order to determine the utilization of the Website and Application or to make improvements.</p>\r\n<p>12.5 The IP address of your computer will only be stored for the duration of your visit and will subsequently be deleted immediately or made anonymous by shortening it. The remaining personal data is stored anonymously for an unlimited period of time.</p>\r\n<p>12.6 The personal data will be deleted as soon as you close our Application.</p>\r\n<p>12.7 The privacy of children is one of our concerns. Here at BRIZ we can provide services only in case you are aged 16 or older. If you are under 16 you will need to get your parent’s/guardian’s permission before submission of any personal data to BRIZ. If you are underage, and there are no data as to your parent’s/guardian’s permission to use our Website and Application, we will not collect or process your personal data, and you will have limited/restricted use of our Website and Application.</p>\r\n<p><b>13. Cookies</b></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-bottom: 0in;\" align=\"RIGHT\"><i>We explain here what cookies are, how we use cookies, your choices regarding cookies and further information about cookies.</i></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>13.1 Does BRIZ use cookies?</p>\r\n<p>Yes. BRIZ uses cookies and other technologies on our Website and within our related services. By using our Website or our related services, you consent to the use of cookies for the purposes we describe in this policy.</p>\r\n<p>13.2 What are cookies and how do they work?</p>\r\n<p>Cookies are small files comprising bits of text that are installed on your computer or mobile device each time you open a Website. These small files enable users to authenticate themselves on successive visits to the Website and gain access to the services.</p>\r\n<p>Your browser tells our systems if any cookies files were installed in your computer and after our software systems connect to the cookies we are able to analyze the information the cookies files give us.</p>\r\n<p>13.3 What cookies does BRIZ use and for what purposes?</p>\r\n<p>We use the personal data we process using technically unnecessary cookies to tailor our Website to your individual interests. This includes, for example, advertising that corresponds to your personal interests.</p>\r\n<p>13.4 What is the duration of cookies storage with BRIZ?</p>\r\n<p>The duration of storage varies depending on whether the cookies are session cookies or temporary cookies. Session cookies are automatically deleted after you leave our Website. Temporary cookies are stored on your device for a certain period. Cookies that we use for statistical purposes are automatically deleted after a defined period.</p>\r\n<p>13.5 Can I opt-out from the use of cookies after I agreed BRIZ will use it?</p>\r\n<p>No, you may not opt-out from the session cookies used within the use.</p>\r\n<p>13.6 What are your choices regarding cookies</p>\r\n<p>As a user, you have full control over the use of cookies and the personal data processed in this way. If you do not want to use cookies, you can set your browser so that the storage of cookies will not be accepted. Please note that in this case, you may be able to use our Website only partially or not at all.</p>\r\n<p>13.7 Finally, please be informed that you have the right to withdraw your consent so that we cannot use cookies, setting your browser in the terms mentioned below:</p>\r\n<p>- If you use Microsoft Internet Explorer, in the menu option Tools, selecting Internet Options and accessing Privacy; For the Internet Explorer web browser, please visit this page from Microsoft: <a href=\"http://support.microsoft.com/kb/278835\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>http://support.microsoft.com/kb/278835</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>- If you use Firefox for Mac in the Preferences menu option, selecting Privacy, accessing the Show Cookies section, and in the Tools menu option, selecting Options, accessing Privacy and then using a custom configuration for the history; For the Firefox web browser, please visit this page from Mozilla: <a href=\"https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/delete-cookies-remove-info-websites-stored\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/delete-cookies-remove-info-websites-stored</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>- If you use Safari, in the Preferences menu option, selecting Privacy;</p>\r\n<p>For the Safari web browser, please visit this page from Apple: <a href=\"https://support.apple.com/kb/PH21411?locale=en_US\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://support.apple.com/kb/PH21411?locale=en_US</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>- If you use Google Chrome, in the Tools menu option, selecting Options (Preferences in Mac), accessing Advanced and then in the Content Configuration option in the Privacy section, and finally checking Cookies in the Content Settings dialogue; For the Chrome web browser, please visit this page from Google: <a href=\"https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/32050\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>https://support.google.com/accounts/answer/32050</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>For any other web browser, please visit your web browser\'s official web pages.</p>\r\n<p>13.8 Where can you find more information about cookies?</p>\r\n<p>You can learn more about cookies and the following third-party websites:</p>\r\n<p>AllAboutCookies: <a href=\"http://www.allaboutcookies.org/\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>http://www.allaboutcookies.org/</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p>Network Advertising Initiative: <a href=\"http://www.networkadvertising.org/\"><span style=\"color: #1155cc;\"><u>http://www.networkadvertising.org/</u></span></a>.</p>\r\n<p><b>14. Personal Data Security</b></p>\r\n<p>14.1 We protect our Website and Application and other systems by technical and organizational measures against loss, destruction, access, modification, or dissemination of your personal data by unauthorized persons. These measures include but are not limited to access control, input control and order control.</p>\r\n<p>14.2 BRIZ processes your personal data using computers and/or other IT enabled tools. BRIZ takes technical and organizational measures to ensure the information is processed in a manner that ensures appropriate security of information, including protection against unauthorized or unlawful processing and against accidental loss, destruction or damage. We also guide and train our personnel to process your personal data securely according to our internal personal data protection policies.</p>\r\n<p><b>15. No Disclosure of Your Personal Data</b></p>\r\n<p>We will not disclose your personal data to third parties, except if you have consented to the personal data transfer or if we are authorized or obliged to transfer personal data due to legal provisions and/or official or court directions. This may refer to cases including but not limited to the provision of information for the purposes of law enforcement, danger prevention or the enforcement of intellectual property rights.</p>\r\n<p><b>16. Personal Data Protection and Third-Party Websites</b></p>\r\n<p>16.1 This Website may contain hyperlinks to or from third-party websites. If you follow a hyperlink to one of these websites, please note that we cannot assume any responsibility or guarantee for external contents or personal data protection conditions. Please verify the respective applicable data protection provisions before you transfer personal data to these websites.</p>\r\n<p>16.2 Personal data communication via the internet cannot be guaranteed to be error-free and/or available at all times according to the current state of technology. In this respect, we are not liable for the constant and uninterrupted availability of our trading system.</p>\r\n<p><b>17. Amendments</b></p>\r\n<p>We reserve the right to amend this Privacy Policy at any time with future effect. The respective latest version is available at all time on the Website and the Application. Please access the Website and Application regularly to find out about the applicable Privacy Policy.</p>\r\n<p><b>18. Your Rights and Contact Information</b></p>\r\n<p>18.1 Right to withdraw your consent acc. Art. 7 para. 3 GDPR: In cases where the processing of your personal data is only possible with your consent, you can revoke this consent at any time in the future. \"For the Future\" means that your revocation has no effect on the processing of personal data that we have made between the granting of your consent and your revocation. You do not have to justify your withdrawal. An informal message via e-mail to us is sufficient.</p>\r\n<p>18.2 Right of access by the data subject in acc. Art. 15 GDPR: you may request confirmation from us at any time whether we process personal information concerning you. In this case, you have the right to request information about:</p>\r\n<p>- the purposes for which we process your personal information</p>\r\n<p>- the categories of personal data we process,</p>\r\n<p>- the recipients or categories of recipients to whom we have disclosed or will disclose the personal data,</p>\r\n<p>- the storage duration (as far as possible),</p>\r\n<p>- the right of rectification, erasure or restriction of our processing, as well as the right of opposition to such processing,</p>\r\n<p>- the existence of a right of appeal to a supervisory authority,</p>\r\n<p>- the origin of your personal data, as far as they were not collected by us,</p>\r\n<p>- the existence of automated decision-making including profiling and, where appropriate, detailed information on the logic, scope and impact of such processing.</p>\r\n<p>For this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.</p>\r\n<p>18.3 Right to rectification acc. Art. 16 GDPR: you can view your personal data at any time free of charge and, if necessary, request their correction and supplementation.</p>\r\n<p>For this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app.. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.</p>\r\n<p>18.4 Right to erasure acc. Art. 17 GDPR: you can view your personal data at any time free of charge and request cancellation if:</p>\r\n<p>- these are no longer needed for the purpose for which they were processed,</p>\r\n<p>- you have revoked your consent and there is no other legal basis for the processing,</p>\r\n<p>- you have filed an objection against the processing of your personal data acc. Art. 21 GDPR,</p>\r\n<p>- we have processed your personal data unlawfully,</p>\r\n<p>- the deletion is required to fulfil a legal obligation under EU or national law.</p>\r\n<p>For this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.</p>\r\n<p>18.5 Right to the restriction of processing acc. Art. 18 GDPR: you can view your personal data at any time free of charge and, if necessary, request their blocking if:</p>\r\n<p>- you deny their accuracy,</p>\r\n<p>- the processing is illegal, but you reject the deletion of the personal data,</p>\r\n<p>- we no longer need the personal data, but you need it for the assertion, exercise or defence of legal claims,</p>\r\n<p>- you have filed an objection against the processing of your personal data acc. Art. 21 GDPR, but it is not yet certain whether our interests in processing outweigh your interests.</p>\r\n<p>For this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.</p>\r\n<p>18.6 Right to data portability acc. Art. 20 GDPR: At our request, we are required to provide you with data that we process automatically based on your consent or in fulfilment of a contract in a portable and secure format. The direct transfer of personal data to another person responsible is also possible at your request. However, it only takes place if technically feasible.</p>\r\n<p>For this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.</p>\r\n<p>18.7 Right to object acc. Art. 21 GDPR: In cases where we use your personal data on the basis of Art. 6 para. 1 lit. f GDPR, you have the right to appeal against the processing, as far as there are reasons for this, which result from your particular situation or the objection against direct mailing.</p>\r\n<p>For this purpose and / or for more information, please contact us via hello@briz.app. If you have any questions, comments or inquiries regarding the processing of your personal data, please also contact us at the contact details provided.</p>\r\n<p>18.8 Right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority acc. Art. 77 GDPR: If you think that we have violated data protection regulations, you can contact a regulatory authority for personal data protection in the non-public area, in particular, the supervisory authority of your habitual residence, your work-place or the location of such violation.</p>\r\n<p><b>BRIZ Mobility Limited Ltd.</b></p>\r\n<p><b>May 2019</b></p>',	'Privacy Policy',	'',	'inherit',	'closed',	'closed',	'',	'3-revision-v1',	'',	'',	'2019-05-14 17:55:30',	'2019-05-14 14:55:30',	'',	3,	'https://briz.app/3-revision-v1/',	0,	'revision',	'',	0),
